ne\\u2605\\u2605\\u2605\\u2605 \\u201cAn honest, intimate, and emotionally engaging&hellip;\",\"image_url\":\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/c9\\/91dd861e97fee4c86ef483016f9d25\\/w880\\/q80\\/cx110\\/cw425\\/ch426\\/images\\/uploads\\/c991dd861e97fee4c86ef483016f9d25.jpeg\",\"image_source\":\"type=\\\"image\\/webp\\\" srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/c9\\/91dd861e97fee4c86ef483016f9d25\\/w640\\/q80\\/wpojpeg\\/cx110\\/cw425\\/ch426\\/images\\/uploads\\/c991dd861e97fee4c86ef483016f9d25.webp 880w,https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/c9\\/91dd861e97fee4c86ef483016f9d25\\/w640\\/q80\\/wpojpeg\\/cx110\\/cw425\\/ch426\\/images\\/uploads\\/c991dd861e97fee4c86ef483016f9d25.webp 1210w,https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/c9\\/91dd861e97fee4c86ef483016f9d25\\/w640\\/q80\\/wpojpeg\\/cx110\\/cw425\\/ch426\\/images\\/uploads\\/c991dd861e97fee4c86ef483016f9d25.webp 1470w,https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/c9\\/91dd861e97fee4c86ef483016f9d25\\/w640\\/q80\\/wpojpeg\\/cx110\\/cw425\\/ch426\\/images\\/uploads\\/c991dd861e97fee4c86ef483016f9d25.webp 1680w,https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/c9\\/91dd861e97fee4c86ef483016f9d25\\/w640\\/q80\\/wpojpeg\\/cx110\\/cw425\\/ch426\\/images\\/uploads\\/c991dd861e97fee4c86ef483016f9d25.webp 1870w,https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/c9\\/91dd861e97fee4c86ef483016f9d25\\/w640\\/q80\\/wpojpeg\\/cx110\\/cw425\\/ch426\\/images\\/uploads\\/c991dd861e97fee4c86ef483016f9d25.webp 2048w,https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/c9\\/91dd861e97fee4c86ef483016f9d25\\/w640\\/q80\\/wpojpeg\\/cx110\\/cw425\\/ch426\\/images\\/uploads\\/c991dd861e97fee4c86ef483016f9d25.webp 2880w\\\"\",\"image_alt\":\"\",\"image_cap\":\"\",\"image_data\":[\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/c9\\/91dd861e97fee4c86ef483016f9d25\\/w640\\/q80\\/wpojpeg\\/cx110\\/cw425\\/ch426\\/images\\/uploads\\/c991dd861e97fee4c86ef483016f9d25.webp 880w\",\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/c9\\/91dd861e97fee4c86ef483016f9d25\\/w640\\/q80\\/wpojpeg\\/cx110\\/cw425\\/ch426\\/images\\/uploads\\/c991dd861e97fee4c86ef483016f9d25.webp 1210w\",\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/c9\\/91dd861e97fee4c86ef483016f9d25\\/w640\\/q80\\/wpojpeg\\/cx110\\/cw425\\/ch426\\/images\\/uploads\\/c991dd861e97fee4c86ef483016f9d25.webp 1470w\",\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/c9\\/91dd861e97fee4c86ef483016f9d25\\/w640\\/q80\\/wpojpeg\\/cx110\\/cw425\\/ch426\\/images\\/uploads\\/c991dd861e97fee4c86ef483016f9d25.webp 1680w\",\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/c9\\/91dd861e97fee4c86ef483016f9d25\\/w640\\/q80\\/wpojpeg\\/cx110\\/cw425\\/ch426\\/images\\/uploads\\/c991dd861e97fee4c86ef483016f9d25.webp 1870w\",\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/c9\\/91dd861e97fee4c86ef483016f9d25\\/w640\\/q80\\/wpojpeg\\/cx110\\/cw425\\/ch426\\/images\\/uploads\\/c991dd861e97fee4c86ef483016f9d25.webp 2048w\",\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/c9\\/91dd861e97fee4c86ef483016f9d25\\/w640\\/q80\\/wpojpeg\\/cx110\\/cw425\\/ch426\\/images\\/uploads\\/c991dd861e97fee4c86ef483016f9d25.webp 2880w\"],\"focal_point\":[\"51.2\",\"10.4\"],\"search_text\":\"\\u2605\\u2605\\u2605\\u2605\\u2605 Lovers Of Black Theatre\\u2605\\u2605\\u2605\\u2605 \\u201cCarries the production with remarkable control.\\u201d \\u2014 Flicker Magazine\\u2605\\u2605\\u2605\\u2605 \\u201cAn honest, intimate, and emotionally engaging piece of theatre.\\u201d \\u2014 The Theatre Reviewer\\u2605\\u2605\\u2605\\u2605 \\u201cWitty, poignant, and well written.\\u201d \\u2014 Afridiziak Theatre News\\u2605\\u2605\\u2605\\u2605\\u201cA poignant and entertaining performance.\\u201d \\u2014 The Deskbound DramaticTrapped within the four walls of a university bedroom, \\u2018Monkeyface\\u2019 navigates the euphoric highs and crushing lows of Freshers Week, toxic friendships, club culture, and the aching need for connection. What begins as something relatable (flatmates, cliques, and the messy thrill of queer nightlife) slowly unravels into a raw portrait of a young Black Gay student fighting to stay afloat inside a world not built to hold him.\\u00a0CREATIVE TEAM:\\u00a0Writer & Performer: Raphael Phillips\\u00a0Director: Mojola Akinyemi\\u00a0Stage Manager & Lighting Designer: Isha BahAssistant Director & Sound Designer: Joe Harrington\\u00a0Set Designer: Valentina Turtur\\u00a0Producer: BLACKRIOT Productions\\u00a0CONTENT WARNING:\\u00a0This show contains strong language, references to drug use, sexual content and themes of racism and mental health. People under the age of 16 will not be admitted for this show.\\u00a0\",\"book_link\":false,\"event_type\":[\"3\"],\"search\":\"Monkeyface Monkeyface Theatre  <blockquote><p>\\u2605\\u2605\\u2605\\u2605\\u2605 <i>Lovers Of Black Theatre<\\/i><\\/p><p>\\u2605\\u2605\\u2605\\u2605 \\u201cCarries the production with remarkable control.\\u201d \\u2014 <i>Flicker Magazine<\\/i><\\/p><p>\\u2605\\u2605\\u2605\\u2605 \\u201cAn honest, intimate, and emotionally engaging piece of theatre.\\u201d \\u2014 <i>The Theatre Reviewer<\\/i><\\/p><p>\\u2605\\u2605\\u2605\\u2605 \\u201cWitty, poignant, and well written.\\u201d \\u2014 <i>Afridiziak Theatre News<\\/i><\\/p><p>\\u2605\\u2605\\u2605\\u2605\\u201cA poignant and entertaining performance.\\u201d \\u2014 <i>The Deskbound Dramatic<\\/i><\\/p><\\/blockquote><p>Trapped within the four walls of a university bedroom, \\u2018Monkeyface\\u2019 navigates the euphoric highs and crushing lows of Freshers Week, toxic friendships, club culture, and the aching need for connection. What begins as something relatable (flatmates, cliques, and the messy thrill of queer nightlife) slowly unravels into a raw portrait of a young Black Gay student fighting to stay afloat inside a world not built to hold him.<\\/p><p>&nbsp;<\\/p><p><strong>CREATIVE TEAM:&nbsp;<\\/strong><\\/p><p>Writer &amp; Performer: Raphael Phillips&nbsp;<\\/p><p>Director: Mojola Akinyemi&nbsp;<\\/p><p>Stage Manager &amp; Lighting Designer: Isha Bah<\\/p><p>Assistant Director &amp; Sound Designer: Joe Harrington&nbsp;<\\/p><p>Set Designer: Valentina Turtur&nbsp;<\\/p><p>Producer: BLACKRIOT Productions<\\/p><p>&nbsp;<\\/p><p><strong>CONTENT WARNING:&nbsp;<\\/strong><\\/p><p>This show contains strong language, references to drug use, sexual content and themes of racism and mental health. People under the age of 16 will not be admitted for this show.&nbsp;<\\/p> Monkeyface  \\u2605\\u2605\\u2605\\u2605\\u2605 Lovers Of Black Theatre\\u2605\\u2605\\u2605\\u2605 \\u201cCarries the production with remarkable control.\\u201d \\u2014 Flicker Magazine\\u2605\\u2605\\u2605\\u2605 \\u201cAn honest, intimate, and emotionally engaging piece of theatre.\\u201d \\u2014 The Theatre Reviewer\\u2605\\u2605\\u2605\\u2605 \\u201cWitty, poignant, and well written.\\u201d \\u2014 Afridiziak Theatre News\\u2605\\u2605\\u2605\\u2605\\u201cA poignant and entertaining performance.\\u201d \\u2014 The Deskbound DramaticTrapped within the four walls of a university bedroom, \\u2018Monkeyface\\u2019 navigates the euphoric highs and crushing lows of Freshers Week, toxic friendships, club culture, and the aching need for connection. What begins as something relatable (flatmates, cliques, and the messy thrill of queer nightlife) slowly unravels into a raw portrait of a young Black Gay student fighting to stay afloat inside a world not built to hold him.\\u00a0CREATIVE TEAM:\\u00a0Writer & Performer: Raphael Phillips\\u00a0Director: Mojola Akinyemi\\u00a0Stage Manager & Lighting Designer: Isha BahAssistant Director & Sound Designer: Joe Harrington\\u00a0Set Designer: Valentina Turtur\\u00a0Producer: BLACKRIOT Productions\\u00a0CONTENT WARNING:\\u00a0This show contains strong language, references to drug use, sexual content and themes of racism and mental health. People under the age of 16 will not be admitted for this show.\\u00a0 Theatre\"},{\"url\":\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/whats-on\\/uwk-bitesize-exhibition\\/\",\"id\":\"4255\",\"name\":\"Bitesize Exhibition\",\"title\":\"Bitesize Exhibition\",\"duration\":\"\",\"slot_tag\":\"Art & Exhibitions\",\"link_title\":\"More Info\",\"performances\":{\"0\":[{\"tag_ids\":[\"81021\",\"55\"],\"tag_name\":\"\",\"html\":\"\"}]},\"performance_dates\":[],\"times\":[],\"start_date\":\"1783440000\",\"end_date\":\"1788120000\",\"age_rating_class\":\"\",\"ticket_free\":false,\"priority_booking\":true,\"hash\":\"TkRRaTVlTFF3TW1TTHNJNm9ZZHAzdz09\",\"embed_id\":\"\",\"embed_host\":\"\",\"date_formatted\":\"Tue 7 Jul - Sun 30 Aug 2026\",\"text\":\"7 JULY - 30 AUGUST&nbsp;A vibrant new group exhibition, Bitesize Exhibition, opens on 6 July, bringing together up to 15 artists and more than 40 works&hellip;\",\"image_url\":\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/9d\\/2ab015ed87b07980ef64ebbb89f8e8\\/w880\\/q80\\/images\\/uploads\\/9d2ab015ed87b07980ef64ebbb89f8e8.png\",\"image_source\":\"type=\\\"image\\/webp\\\" srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/9d\\/2ab015ed87b07980ef64ebbb89f8e8\\/w880\\/q80\\/wpopng\\/images\\/uploads\\/9d2ab015ed87b07980ef64ebbb89f8e8.webp 880w,https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/9d\\/2ab015ed87b07980ef64ebbb89f8e8\\/w1210\\/q80\\/wpopng\\/images\\/uploads\\/9d2ab015ed87b07980ef64ebbb89f8e8.webp 1210w,https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/9d\\/2ab015ed87b07980ef64ebbb89f8e8\\/w1470\\/q80\\/wpopng\\/images\\/uploads\\/9d2ab015ed87b07980ef64ebbb89f8e8.webp 1470w,https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/9d\\/2ab015ed87b07980ef64ebbb89f8e8\\/w1680\\/q80\\/wpopng\\/images\\/uploads\\/9d2ab015ed87b07980ef64ebbb89f8e8.webp 1680w,https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/9d\\/2ab015ed87b07980ef64ebbb89f8e8\\/w1755\\/q80\\/wpopng\\/images\\/uploads\\/9d2ab015ed87b07980ef64ebbb89f8e8.webp 1870w,https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/9d\\/2ab015ed87b07980ef64ebbb89f8e8\\/w1755\\/q80\\/wpopng\\/images\\/uploads\\/9d2ab015ed87b07980ef64ebbb89f8e8.webp 2048w,https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/9d\\/2ab015ed87b07980ef64ebbb89f8e8\\/w1755\\/q80\\/wpopng\\/images\\/uploads\\/9d2ab015ed87b07980ef64ebbb89f8e8.webp 2880w\\\"\",\"image_alt\":\"\",\"image_cap\":\"\",\"image_data\":[\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/9d\\/2ab015ed87b07980ef64ebbb89f8e8\\/w880\\/q80\\/wpopng\\/images\\/uploads\\/9d2ab015ed87b07980ef64ebbb89f8e8.webp 880w\",\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/9d\\/2ab015ed87b07980ef64ebbb89f8e8\\/w1210\\/q80\\/wpopng\\/images\\/uploads\\/9d2ab015ed87b07980ef64ebbb89f8e8.webp 1210w\",\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/9d\\/2ab015ed87b07980ef64ebbb89f8e8\\/w1470\\/q80\\/wpopng\\/images\\/uploads\\/9d2ab015ed87b07980ef64ebbb89f8e8.webp 1470w\",\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/9d\\/2ab015ed87b07980ef64ebbb89f8e8\\/w1680\\/q80\\/wpopng\\/images\\/uploads\\/9d2ab015ed87b07980ef64ebbb89f8e8.webp 1680w\",\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/9d\\/2ab015ed87b07980ef64ebbb89f8e8\\/w1755\\/q80\\/wpopng\\/images\\/uploads\\/9d2ab015ed87b07980ef64ebbb89f8e8.webp 1870w\",\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/9d\\/2ab015ed87b07980ef64ebbb89f8e8\\/w1755\\/q80\\/wpopng\\/images\\/uploads\\/9d2ab015ed87b07980ef64ebbb89f8e8.webp 2048w\",\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/9d\\/2ab015ed87b07980ef64ebbb89f8e8\\/w1755\\/q80\\/wpopng\\/images\\/uploads\\/9d2ab015ed87b07980ef64ebbb89f8e8.webp 2880w\"],\"focal_point\":[\"50\",\"50\"],\"search_text\":\"7 JULY - 30 AUGUST\\u00a0A vibrant new group exhibition, Bitesize Exhibition, opens on 6 July, bringing together up to 15 artists and more than 40 works across a diverse range of mediums, styles, and subject matter as part of Bitesize festival 50.Running alongside our popular Bitesize Theatre and Cinema programme, the exhibition celebrates creativity in all its forms, offering visitors the chance to experience a collection of contemporary art. From painting and photography to installation, and mixed media, the exhibition showcases a broad spectrum of artistic approaches and ideas.To celebrate the exhibition, a special launch party will take place on 8 August, featuring live installation artwork, music, and the opportunity to connect with participating artists and fellow art enthusiasts.Bitesize Exhibition presents a snapshot of contemporary creative practice, highlighting both emerging and established artists while creating an accessible platform for artistic exchange and discovery.\\u00a0EXHIBITION LAUNCH PARTY: 8 AUGUST\\u00a0ARTISTS:Daria Hlazatova\\u00a0Laurel Gregory\\u00a0Beatrice Raggio\\u00a0Lucy Price\\u00a0Emma Lucia Reyes\\u00a0SuBluEva Pagliari\\u00a0Alice ParsloeAndrea Tierney\\u00a0Rebeca Romeo\\u00a0Laura Gompertz\\u00a0Kai T PearsonAlec Dent\\u00a0Erinn FortsonSam McGounRosa LuetchfordJan UrbanskiLenny Bailleux\",\"book_link\":\"no-link\",\"event_type\":[\"81021\",\"55\"],\"search\":\"Bitesize Exhibition Bitesize Exhibition Art & Exhibitions  <p><strong>7 JULY - 30 AUGUST<\\/strong><\\/p><p>&nbsp;<\\/p><p>A vibrant new group exhibition, Bitesize Exhibition, opens on 6 July, bringing together up to 15 artists and more than 40 works across a diverse range of mediums, styles, and subject matter as part of <a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/bitesize-festival\\/bitesize-festival-2026\\/\\\">Bitesize festival 50<\\/a>.<\\/p><p>Running alongside our popular <a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/bitesize-festival\\/bitesize-festival-2026\\/\\\">Bitesize Theatre <\\/a>and <a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/bitesize-festival\\/bitesize-short-film-festival-2026\\/\\\">Cinema programme,<\\/a> the exhibition celebrates creativity in all its forms, offering visitors the chance to experience a collection of contemporary art. From painting and photography to installation, and mixed media, the exhibition showcases a broad spectrum of artistic approaches and ideas.<\\/p><p>To celebrate the exhibition, a special launch party will take place on 8 August, featuring live installation artwork, music, and the opportunity to connect with participating artists and fellow art enthusiasts.<\\/p><p>Bitesize Exhibition presents a snapshot of contemporary creative practice, highlighting both emerging and established artists while creating an accessible platform for artistic exchange and discovery.<\\/p><p>&nbsp;<\\/p><p><strong>EXHIBITION LAUNCH PARTY: 8 AUGUST<\\/strong><\\/p><p>&nbsp;<\\/p><h3><strong>ARTISTS:<\\/strong><\\/h3><p><strong>Daria Hlazatova&nbsp;<\\/strong><\\/p><p><strong>Laurel Gregory&nbsp;<\\/strong><\\/p><p><strong>Beatrice Raggio&nbsp;<\\/strong><\\/p><p><strong>Lucy Price&nbsp;<\\/strong><\\/p><p><strong>Emma Lucia Reyes&nbsp;<\\/strong><\\/p><p><strong>SuBlu<\\/strong><\\/p><p><strong>Eva Pagliari&nbsp;<\\/strong><\\/p><p><strong>Alice Parsloe<\\/strong><\\/p><p><strong>Andrea Tierney&nbsp;<\\/strong><\\/p><p><strong>Rebeca Romeo&nbsp;<\\/strong><\\/p><p><strong>Laura Gompertz&nbsp;<\\/strong><\\/p><p><strong>Kai T Pearson<\\/strong><\\/p><p><strong>Alec Dent&nbsp;<\\/strong><\\/p><p><strong>Erinn Fortson<\\/strong><\\/p><p><strong>Sam McGoun<\\/strong><\\/p><p><strong>Rosa Luetchford<\\/strong><\\/p><p><strong>Jan Urbanski<\\/strong><\\/p><p><strong>Lenny Bailleux<\\/strong><\\/p>   7 JULY - 30 AUGUST\\u00a0A vibrant new group exhibition, Bitesize Exhibition, opens on 6 July, bringing together up to 15 artists and more than 40 works across a diverse range of mediums, styles, and subject matter as part of Bitesize festival 50.Running alongside our popular Bitesize Theatre and Cinema programme, the exhibition celebrates creativity in all its forms, offering visitors the chance to experience a collection of contemporary art. From painting and photography to installation, and mixed media, the exhibition showcases a broad spectrum of artistic approaches and ideas.To celebrate the exhibition, a special launch party will take place on 8 August, featuring live installation artwork, music, and the opportunity to connect with participating artists and fellow art enthusiasts.Bitesize Exhibition presents a snapshot of contemporary creative practice, highlighting both emerging and established artists while creating an accessible platform for artistic exchange and discovery.\\u00a0EXHIBITION LAUNCH PARTY: 8 AUGUST\\u00a0ARTISTS:Daria Hlazatova\\u00a0Laurel Gregory\\u00a0Beatrice Raggio\\u00a0Lucy Price\\u00a0Emma Lucia Reyes\\u00a0SuBluEva Pagliari\\u00a0Alice ParsloeAndrea Tierney\\u00a0Rebeca Romeo\\u00a0Laura Gompertz\\u00a0Kai T PearsonAlec Dent\\u00a0Erinn FortsonSam McGounRosa LuetchfordJan UrbanskiLenny Bailleux Bitesize Art & Exhibitions\"},{\"url\":\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/whats-on\\/uws-the-last-one-for-the-road\\/\",\"id\":\"4250\",\"name\":\"The Last One for the Road\",\"title\":\"The Last One for the Road\",\"duration\":\"100 minutes\",\"slot_tag\":\"Cinema\",\"link_title\":\"More Info\",\"performances\":{\"1783810800\":[{\"tag_ids\":[\"101\",\"81000\"],\"tag_name\":\"\",\"html\":\"<a class=\\\"performance button\\\" href=\\\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/seats\\/266201\\/\\\">\\n   \\n      <div class=\\\"performance-time\\\" data-acc=\\\"\\\">16:15<\\/div>\\n    \\n<\\/a>\\n\",\"timestamp\":\"1783869300\",\"accessibility_class\":\"\"}],\"1783897200\":[{\"tag_ids\":[\"101\",\"81000\"],\"tag_name\":\"\",\"html\":\"<a class=\\\"performance button\\\" href=\\\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/seats\\/266401\\/\\\">\\n   \\n      <div class=\\\"performance-time\\\" data-acc=\\\"\\\">13:00<\\/div>\\n    \\n<\\/a>\\n\",\"timestamp\":\"1783944000\",\"accessibility_class\":\"\"}],\"1783983600\":[{\"tag_ids\":[\"101\",\"81000\"],\"tag_name\":\"\",\"html\":\"<a class=\\\"performance button\\\" href=\\\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/seats\\/266601\\/\\\">\\n   \\n      <div class=\\\"performance-time\\\" data-acc=\\\"\\\">18:00<\\/div>\\n    \\n<\\/a>\\n\",\"timestamp\":\"1784048400\",\"accessibility_class\":\"\"}]},\"performance_dates\":[1783810800,1783897200,1783983600],\"times\":[1783869300,1783944000,1784048400],\"start_date\":\"1783869300\",\"end_date\":\"1784048400\",\"age_rating_class\":\"15\",\"ticket_free\":false,\"priority_booking\":true,\"hash\":\"SEhSUEVYUGdVMXZCSFQ3UUx5c0VIdz09\",\"embed_id\":\"\",\"embed_host\":\"\",\"date_formatted\":\"Sun 12 - Tue 14 Jul 2026\",\"text\":\"\\u201cLoosely reminiscent of the happy-sad fables of Alice Rohrwacher, Francesco Sossai\\u2019s boozy dramedy is enchanting\\u201d - Tomris Laffly, Variety\\\" a leisurely&hellip;\",\"image_url\":\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/3d\\/84011edba3d9f1ac1e142d8bfea407\\/w880\\/q80\\/cx731\\/cw1039\\/ch1040\\/images\\/uploads\\/3d84011edba3d9f1ac1e142d8bfea407.jpg\",\"image_source\":\"type=\\\"image\\/webp\\\" srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/3d\\/84011edba3d9f1ac1e142d8bfea407\\/w880\\/q80\\/wpojpg\\/cx731\\/cw1039\\/ch1040\\/images\\/uploads\\/3d84011edba3d9f1ac1e142d8bfea407.webp 880w,https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/3d\\/84011edba3d9f1ac1e142d8bfea407\\/w1210\\/q80\\/wpojpg\\/cx731\\/cw1039\\/ch1040\\/images\\/uploads\\/3d84011edba3d9f1ac1e142d8bfea407.webp 1210w,https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/3d\\/84011edba3d9f1ac1e142d8bfea407\\/w1470\\/q80\\/wpojpg\\/cx731\\/cw1039\\/ch1040\\/images\\/uploads\\/3d84011edba3d9f1ac1e142d8bfea407.webp 1470w,https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/3d\\/84011edba3d9f1ac1e142d8bfea407\\/w1680\\/q80\\/wpojpg\\/cx731\\/cw1039\\/ch1040\\/images\\/uploads\\/3d84011edba3d9f1ac1e142d8bfea407.webp 1680w,https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/3d\\/84011edba3d9f1ac1e142d8bfea407\\/w1870\\/q80\\/wpojpg\\/cx731\\/cw1039\\/ch1040\\/images\\/uploads\\/3d84011edba3d9f1ac1e142d8bfea407.webp 1870w,https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/3d\\/84011edba3d9f1ac1e142d8bfea407\\/w1998\\/q80\\/wpojpg\\/cx731\\/cw1039\\/ch1040\\/images\\/uploads\\/3d84011edba3d9f1ac1e142d8bfea407.webp 2048w,https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/3d\\/84011edba3d9f1ac1e142d8bfea407\\/w1998\\/q80\\/wpojpg\\/cx731\\/cw1039\\/ch1040\\/images\\/uploads\\/3d84011edba3d9f1ac1e142d8bfea407.webp 2880w\\\"\",\"image_alt\":\"\",\"image_cap\":\"\",\"image_data\":[\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/3d\\/84011edba3d9f1ac1e142d8bfea407\\/w880\\/q80\\/wpojpg\\/cx731\\/cw1039\\/ch1040\\/images\\/uploads\\/3d84011edba3d9f1ac1e142d8bfea407.webp 880w\",\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/3d\\/84011edba3d9f1ac1e142d8bfea407\\/w1210\\/q80\\/wpojpg\\/cx731\\/cw1039\\/ch1040\\/images\\/uploads\\/3d84011edba3d9f1ac1e142d8bfea407.webp 1210w\",\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/3d\\/84011edba3d9f1ac1e142d8bfea407\\/w1470\\/q80\\/wpojpg\\/cx731\\/cw1039\\/ch1040\\/images\\/uploads\\/3d84011edba3d9f1ac1e142d8bfea407.webp 1470w\",\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/3d\\/84011edba3d9f1ac1e142d8bfea407\\/w1680\\/q80\\/wpojpg\\/cx731\\/cw1039\\/ch1040\\/images\\/uploads\\/3d84011edba3d9f1ac1e142d8bfea407.webp 1680w\",\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/3d\\/84011edba3d9f1ac1e142d8bfea407\\/w1870\\/q80\\/wpojpg\\/cx731\\/cw1039\\/ch1040\\/images\\/uploads\\/3d84011edba3d9f1ac1e142d8bfea407.webp 1870w\",\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/3d\\/84011edba3d9f1ac1e142d8bfea407\\/w1998\\/q80\\/wpojpg\\/cx731\\/cw1039\\/ch1040\\/images\\/uploads\\/3d84011edba3d9f1ac1e142d8bfea407.webp 2048w\",\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/3d\\/84011edba3d9f1ac1e142d8bfea407\\/w1998\\/q80\\/wpojpg\\/cx731\\/cw1039\\/ch1040\\/images\\/uploads\\/3d84011edba3d9f1ac1e142d8bfea407.webp 2880w\"],\"focal_point\":[\"50\",\"50\"],\"search_text\":\"\\u201cLoosely reminiscent of the happy-sad fables of Alice Rohrwacher, Francesco Sossai\\u2019s boozy dramedy is enchanting\\u201d - Tomris Laffly, Variety\\\" a leisurely Beckettian bender through northeastern Italy\\\" - BFI Sight & Sound MagazineWorld Premiere: CANNES FILM FESTIVAL - Un Certain Regard 2025Surviving bar-to-bar on anecdotes and the \\u2018good old days\\u2019, two blustery 50-somethings hatch a plan to change their luck by digging up the cash their old pal buried before he left for Argentina. En route to the airport, they come across a shy architecture student whose view of life will transform as they take him under their wing on a road trip across the Venetian plains.THE LAST ONE FOR THE ROAD is the award-winning, critically-acclaimed, festival-favourite, boozy road movie you didn\\u2019t know you needed this summer. Take a trip across Northern Italy with this charming adventure including fabulous performances by Filippo Scotti (The Hand of God), Sergio Romano, and Pierpaolo Capovilla.Age Rating:15Language:Italian with subtitlesContent Warnings:strong language, brief drug misuse, nudityDirector:Francesco SossaiCast:Filippo Scotti, Sergio Romano, Pierpaolo Capovilla, Roberto Citran, Andrea PennacchiCompany:Bulldog Film DistributionTrailers:20 minsYear of Release:2026\",\"book_link\":false,\"event_age_ratings\":[\"81000\"],\"event_type\":[\"101\"],\"search\":\"The Last One for the Road The Last One for the Road Cinema  <blockquote><p>\\u201cLoosely reminiscent of the happy-sad fables of Alice Rohrwacher, Francesco Sossai\\u2019s boozy dramedy is enchanting\\u201d - Tomris Laffly, Variety<\\/p><p>\\\" a leisurely Beckettian bender through northeastern Italy\\\" - BFI Sight &amp; Sound Magazine<\\/p><\\/blockquote><h3>World Premiere: CANNES FILM FESTIVAL - Un Certain Regard 2025<\\/h3><p>Surviving bar-to-bar on anecdotes and the \\u2018good old days\\u2019, two blustery 50-somethings hatch a plan to change their luck by digging up the cash their old pal buried before he left for Argentina. En route to the airport, they come across a shy architecture student whose view of life will transform as they take him under their wing on a road trip across the Venetian plains.<\\/p><p><i><strong>THE LAST ONE FOR THE ROAD<\\/strong><\\/i> is the award-winning, critically-acclaimed, festival-favourite, boozy road movie you didn\\u2019t know you needed this summer. Take a trip across Northern Italy with this charming adventure including fabulous performances by Filippo Scotti (<i>The Hand of God<\\/i>), Sergio Romano, and Pierpaolo Capovilla.<\\/p><figure class=\\\"table\\\"><table><tbody><tr><td><strong>Age Rating:<\\/strong><\\/td><td>15<\\/td><\\/tr><tr><td><strong>Language:<\\/strong><\\/td><td>Italian with subtitles<\\/td><\\/tr><tr><td><strong>Content Warnings:<\\/strong><\\/td><td>strong language, brief drug misuse, nudity<\\/td><\\/tr><tr><td><strong>Director:<\\/strong><\\/td><td>Francesco Sossai<\\/td><\\/tr><tr><td><strong>Cast:<\\/strong><\\/td><td>Filippo Scotti, Sergio Romano, Pierpaolo Capovilla, Roberto Citran, Andrea Pennacchi<\\/td><\\/tr><tr><td><strong>Company:<\\/strong><\\/td><td>Bulldog Film Distribution<\\/td><\\/tr><tr><td><strong>Trailers:<\\/strong><\\/td><td>20 mins<\\/td><\\/tr><tr><td><strong>Year of Release:<\\/strong><\\/td><td>2026<\\/td><\\/tr><\\/tbody><\\/table><\\/figure> The Last One for the Road  \\u201cLoosely reminiscent of the happy-sad fables of Alice Rohrwacher, Francesco Sossai\\u2019s boozy dramedy is enchanting\\u201d - Tomris Laffly, Variety\\\" a leisurely Beckettian bender through northeastern Italy\\\" - BFI Sight & Sound MagazineWorld Premiere: CANNES FILM FESTIVAL - Un Certain Regard 2025Surviving bar-to-bar on anecdotes and the \\u2018good old days\\u2019, two blustery 50-somethings hatch a plan to change their luck by digging up the cash their old pal buried before he left for Argentina. En route to the airport, they come across a shy architecture student whose view of life will transform as they take him under their wing on a road trip across the Venetian plains.THE LAST ONE FOR THE ROAD is the award-winning, critically-acclaimed, festival-favourite, boozy road movie you didn\\u2019t know you needed this summer. Take a trip across Northern Italy with this charming adventure including fabulous performances by Filippo Scotti (The Hand of God), Sergio Romano, and Pierpaolo Capovilla.Age Rating:15Language:Italian with subtitlesContent Warnings:strong language, brief drug misuse, nudityDirector:Francesco SossaiCast:Filippo Scotti, Sergio Romano, Pierpaolo Capovilla, Roberto Citran, Andrea PennacchiCompany:Bulldog Film DistributionTrailers:20 minsYear of Release:2026 15 Cinema\"},{\"url\":\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/whats-on\\/uwN-rosebush-pruning\\/\",\"id\":\"4227\",\"name\":\"Rosebush Pruning\",\"title\":\"Rosebush Pruning\",\"duration\":\"94 minutes\",\"slot_tag\":\"Cinema\",\"link_title\":\"More Info\",\"performances\":{\"1783724400\":[{\"tag_ids\":[\"101\",\"80998\",\"80879\"],\"tag_name\":\"\",\"html\":\"<a class=\\\"performance button\\\" href=\\\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/seats\\/264602\\/\\\">\\n   \\n      <div class=\\\"performance-time\\\" data-acc=\\\"\\\">21:00<\\/div>\\n    \\n<\\/a>\\n\",\"timestamp\":\"1783800000\",\"accessibility_class\":\"\"}],\"1783810800\":[{\"tag_ids\":[\"101\",\"80998\",\"80879\"],\"tag_name\":\"\",\"html\":\"<a class=\\\"performance button\\\" href=\\\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/seats\\/264801\\/\\\">\\n   \\n      <div class=\\\"performance-time\\\" data-acc=\\\"\\\">12:00<\\/div>\\n    \\n<\\/a>\\n\",\"timestamp\":\"1783854000\",\"accessibility_class\":\"\"},{\"tag_ids\":[\"101\",\"80998\",\"80879\"],\"tag_name\":\"\",\"html\":\"<a class=\\\"performance button\\\" href=\\\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/seats\\/264802\\/\\\">\\n   \\n      <