\\/custom\\/06\\/c371cde9d1c09945dd273e8d46d9fd\\/w1680\\/q80\\/wpopng\\/cx558\\/cy17\\/cw1426\\/ch1423\\/images\\/uploads\\/06c371cde9d1c09945dd273e8d46d9fd.webp 1680w\",\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/06\\/c371cde9d1c09945dd273e8d46d9fd\\/w1870\\/q80\\/wpopng\\/cx558\\/cy17\\/cw1426\\/ch1423\\/images\\/uploads\\/06c371cde9d1c09945dd273e8d46d9fd.webp 1870w\",\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/06\\/c371cde9d1c09945dd273e8d46d9fd\\/w2048\\/q80\\/wpopng\\/cx558\\/cy17\\/cw1426\\/ch1423\\/images\\/uploads\\/06c371cde9d1c09945dd273e8d46d9fd.webp 2048w\",\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/06\\/c371cde9d1c09945dd273e8d46d9fd\\/w2560\\/q80\\/wpopng\\/cx558\\/cy17\\/cw1426\\/ch1423\\/images\\/uploads\\/06c371cde9d1c09945dd273e8d46d9fd.webp 2880w\"],\"focal_point\":[\"49.7\",\"34.7\"],\"search_text\":\"RIVERSIDE PRIDE Film Season July 2026: enjoy 15% off adult and concessions ticket price offer if you buy more than one ticket to the season in the same order!LOVE ME TENDER (SPECIAL PREVIEW) - From 3 JulyPORTRAIT OF A LADY ON FIRE (RE-RELEASE ) - From 3 JulyTHE BIRDCAGE (30TH ANNIVERSARY) - From 4 JulyCACTUS PEARS - From 10 July\\u00a0We are delighted that director Rohan Parashuram Kanawade has recorded a Q&A for us, which you can see after the end credits finish.WINNER: WORLD CINEMA GRAND JURY PRIZE - SUNDANCE FILM FESTIVAL\\\"A tender queer Indian drama born of grief\\\" - Variety\\\"[a] tender and subtle story of forbidden love and a poignant awakening in India\\u201d \\u2605\\u2605\\u2605\\u2605 GuardianSet in rural Maharashtra, Cactus Pears follows Anand (Bhushaan Manoj), a Mumbai call-centre worker who returns to his ancestral village to observe the ten-day mourning ritual following his father\\u2019s death.While navigating the pressures of family expectations and marriage, he reconnects with Balya (Suraaj Suman), a childhood friend facing similar struggles.Over the course of the mourning period, their bond deepens into a tender and intimate relationship, creating a quiet exploration of grief, identity and queer love within a traditional rural community.Age Rating:15Language:Marathi with English subtitlesContent Warnings:strong language and nudityDirector:Rohan Parashuram KanawadeCast:Bhushaan Manoj, Suraaj Suman, Jayshri JagtapCompany:Lotus Visual ProductionsTrailers:20 minsYear of Release:2026\",\"book_link\":\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/seats\\/245402\\/\",\"cinema\":[\"81023\"],\"event_age_ratings\":[\"81000\"],\"event_type\":[\"101\"],\"search\":\"Cactus Pears + Recorded Director Q&A Cactus Pears + Recorded Director Q&A Cinema  <h3>RIVERSIDE PRIDE Film Season July 2026: enjoy 15% off adult and concessions ticket price offer if you buy more than one ticket to the season in the same order!<\\/h3><p><i>LOVE ME TENDER (SPECIAL PREVIEW)<\\/i> - From 3 July<\\/p><p><i>PORTRAIT OF A LADY ON FIRE (RE-RELEASE<\\/i> ) - From 3 July<\\/p><p><i>THE BIRDCAGE (30TH ANNIVERSARY)<\\/i> - From 4 July<\\/p><p><i>CACTUS PEARS <\\/i>- From 10 July<\\/p><p>&nbsp;<\\/p><h3><strong>We are delighted that director Rohan Parashuram Kanawade has recorded a Q&amp;A for us, which you can see after the end credits finish.<\\/strong><\\/h3><p><strong>WINNER: WORLD CINEMA GRAND JURY PRIZE - SUNDANCE FILM FESTIVAL<\\/strong><\\/p><blockquote><p>\\\"A tender queer Indian drama born of grief\\\" - Variety<\\/p><p>\\\"[a] tender and subtle story of forbidden love and a poignant awakening in India\\u201d \\u2605\\u2605\\u2605\\u2605 Guardian<\\/p><\\/blockquote><p>Set in rural Maharashtra, <i><strong>Cactus Pears<\\/strong><\\/i> follows Anand (Bhushaan Manoj), a Mumbai call-centre worker who returns to his ancestral village to observe the ten-day mourning ritual following his father\\u2019s death.<\\/p><p>While navigating the pressures of family expectations and marriage, he reconnects with Balya (Suraaj Suman), a childhood friend facing similar struggles.<\\/p><p>Over the course of the mourning period, their bond deepens into a tender and intimate relationship, creating a quiet exploration of grief, identity and queer love within a traditional rural community.<\\/p><figure class=\\\"table\\\"><table><tbody><tr><td><strong>Age Rating:<\\/strong><\\/td><td>15<\\/td><\\/tr><tr><td><strong>Language:<\\/strong><\\/td><td>Marathi with English subtitles<\\/td><\\/tr><tr><td><strong>Content Warnings:<\\/strong><\\/td><td>strong language and nudity<\\/td><\\/tr><tr><td><strong>Director:<\\/strong><\\/td><td>Rohan Parashuram Kanawade<\\/td><\\/tr><tr><td><strong>Cast:<\\/strong><\\/td><td>Bhushaan Manoj, Suraaj Suman, Jayshri Jagtap<\\/td><\\/tr><tr><td><strong>Company:<\\/strong><\\/td><td>Lotus Visual Productions<\\/td><\\/tr><tr><td><strong>Trailers:<\\/strong><\\/td><td>20 mins<\\/td><\\/tr><tr><td><strong>Year of Release:<\\/strong><\\/td><td>2026<\\/td><\\/tr><\\/tbody><\\/table><\\/figure> Cactus Pears,Cactus Pears + Recorded Director Q&A  RIVERSIDE PRIDE Film Season July 2026: enjoy 15% off adult and concessions ticket price offer if you buy more than one ticket to the season in the same order!LOVE ME TENDER (SPECIAL PREVIEW) - From 3 JulyPORTRAIT OF A LADY ON FIRE (RE-RELEASE ) - From 3 JulyTHE BIRDCAGE (30TH ANNIVERSARY) - From 4 JulyCACTUS PEARS - From 10 July\\u00a0We are delighted that director Rohan Parashuram Kanawade has recorded a Q&A for us, which you can see after the end credits finish.WINNER: WORLD CINEMA GRAND JURY PRIZE - SUNDANCE FILM FESTIVAL\\\"A tender queer Indian drama born of grief\\\" - Variety\\\"[a] tender and subtle story of forbidden love and a poignant awakening in India\\u201d \\u2605\\u2605\\u2605\\u2605 GuardianSet in rural Maharashtra, Cactus Pears follows Anand (Bhushaan Manoj), a Mumbai call-centre worker who returns to his ancestral village to observe the ten-day mourning ritual following his father\\u2019s death.While navigating the pressures of family expectations and marriage, he reconnects with Balya (Suraaj Suman), a childhood friend facing similar struggles.Over the course of the mourning period, their bond deepens into a tender and intimate relationship, creating a quiet exploration of grief, identity and queer love within a traditional rural community.Age Rating:15Language:Marathi with English subtitlesContent Warnings:strong language and nudityDirector:Rohan Parashuram KanawadeCast:Bhushaan Manoj, Suraaj Suman, Jayshri JagtapCompany:Lotus Visual ProductionsTrailers:20 minsYear of Release:2026 Riverside Pride 15 Cinema\"},{\"url\":\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/whats-on\\/udE-kids-club-tom-and-jerry-the-forbidden-compass\\/\",\"id\":\"4023\",\"name\":\"Kids\\u2019 Club: Tom and Jerry: The Forbidden Compass\",\"title\":\"Kids\\u2019 Club: Tom and Jerry: The Forbidden Compass\",\"duration\":\"100 minutes\",\"slot_tag\":\"Cinema\",\"link_title\":\"More Info\",\"performances\":{\"1783810800\":[{\"tag_ids\":[\"101\",\"81002\",\"81005\",\"80879\"],\"tag_name\":\"\",\"html\":\"<a class=\\\"performance button\\\" href=\\\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/seats\\/251202\\/\\\">\\n   \\n      <div class=\\\"performance-time\\\" data-acc=\\\"\\\">10:30<\\/div>\\n    \\n<\\/a>\\n    <div class=\\\"tooltip\\\" data-tooltip_theme=\\\"#00782A\\\" data-tooltip_text=\\\"Our Kids' Club weekend shows are for budding cinephiles, where all films will be 12A rated or under and at a special price!\\\">Kids' Club<\\/div>\\n\",\"timestamp\":\"1783848600\",\"accessibility_class\":\"\"}]},\"performance_dates\":[1783810800],\"times\":[1783848600],\"start_date\":\"1783848600\",\"end_date\":\"1783848600\",\"age_rating_class\":\"pg\",\"ticket_free\":false,\"priority_booking\":true,\"hash\":\"Ui8rbWhQTkRqRWNxZFpzelVRYWZoQT09\",\"embed_id\":\"\",\"embed_host\":\"\",\"date_formatted\":\"Sun 12 Jul 2026\",\"text\":\"During a chase in a museum, Tom and Jerry accidentally activate a magical compass that transports them to another world.Age Rating:ULanguage:EnglishContent&hellip;\",\"image_