elp her uncover the secrets she\\u2019s searching for? And could the Queen of Hearts cause her to truly lose her head?This \\u201cdelightfully imaginative retelling\\u201d [Broadway World] brings Lewis Carroll\\u2019s much-loved classic to life with \\u201cgorgeous costumes\\u201d [The Times], enchanting puppets, and a kaleidoscope of colourful characters, promising to transport audiences into the fantastical world of Wonderland.Age Rating: Recommended 5+\",\"book_link\":\"no-link\",\"event_type\":[\"3\"],\"search\":\"Alice in Wonderland Alice in Wonderland Theatre  <p>Tumble down the rabbit hole this summer holidays into the fantastical world of Wonderland, where up is down, and nonsense reigns supreme. Join Alice on her unforgettable adventure as she shrinks and grows, meeting peculiar characters at every turn. Who will she encounter next? Will the mischievous Cheshire Cat guide her through the madness? Can the hurried White Rabbit help her uncover the secrets she\\u2019s searching for? And could the Queen of Hearts cause her to truly lose her head?<\\/p><p>This \\u201cdelightfully imaginative retelling\\u201d [Broadway World] brings Lewis Carroll\\u2019s much-loved classic to life with \\u201cgorgeous costumes\\u201d [The Times], enchanting puppets, and a kaleidoscope of colourful characters, promising to transport audiences into the fantastical world of Wonderland.<\\/p><p><strong>Age Rating: Recommended 5+<\\/strong><\\/p>   Tumble down the rabbit hole this summer holidays into the fantastical world of Wonderland, where up is down, and nonsense reigns supreme. Join Alice on her unforgettable adventure as she shrinks and grows, meeting peculiar characters at every turn. Who will she encounter next? Will the mischievous Cheshire Cat guide her through the madness? Can the hurried White Rabbit help her uncover the secrets she\\u2019s searching for? And could the Queen of Hearts cause her to truly lose her head?This \\u201cdelightfully imaginative retelling\\u201d [Broadway World] brings Lewis Carroll\\u2019s much-loved classic to life with \\u201cgorgeous costumes\\u201d [The Times], enchanting puppets, and a kaleidoscope of colourful characters, promising to transport audiences into the fantastical world of Wonderland.Age Rating: Recommended 5+ Theatre\"},{\"url\":\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/whats-on\\/uPT-first-last-dance-a-riverside-rd-sharing\\/\",\"id\":\"4083\",\"name\":\"First Last Dance (A Riverside R&D Sharing)\",\"title\":\"First Last Dance (A Riverside R&D Sharing)\",\"duration\":\"70 minutes\",\"slot_tag\":\"Theatre\",\"link_title\":\"More Info\",\"performances\":{\"1784242800\":[{\"tag_ids\":[\"3\",\"81013\"],\"tag_name\":\"\",\"html\":\"<a class=\\\"performance button\\\" href=\\\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/seats\\/255202\\/\\\">\\n   \\n      <div class=\\\"performance-time\\\" data-acc=\\\"\\\">14:30<\\/div>\\n    \\n<\\/a>\\n\",\"timestamp\":\"1784295000\",\"accessibility_class\":\"\"}]},\"performance_dates\":[1784242800],\"times\":[1784295000],\"start_date\":\"1784295000\",\"end_date\":\"1784295000\",\"age_rating_class\":\"\",\"ticket_free\":false,\"priority_booking\":true,\"hash\":\"TGRkb0RJMSszRkg3Wmw1WHNuZjJqQT09\",\"embed_id\":\"\",\"embed_host\":\"\",\"date_formatted\":\"Fri 17 Jul 2026\",\"text\":\"Two people meet for a drink the night before a criminal trial that will change both their lives forever. First Last Dance&nbsp;is a new play about trust,&hellip;\",\"image_url\":\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/f0\\/794d1407e782b340d96e329389b04f\\/w880\\/q80\\/images\\/uploads\\/f0794d1407e782b340d96e329389b04f.jpg\",\"image_source\":\"type=\\\"image\\/webp\\\" srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/f0\\/794d1407e782b340d96e329389b04f\\/w880\\/q80\\/wpojpg\\/images\\/uploads\\/f0794d1407e782b340d96e329389b04f.webp 880w,https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/f0\\/794d1407e782b340d96e329389b04f\\/w1210\\/q80\\/wpojpg\\/images\\/uploads\\/f0794d1407e782b340d96e329389b04f.webp 1210w,https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/f0\\/794d1407e782b340d96e329389b04f\\/w1470\\/q80\\/wpojpg\\/images\\/uploads\\/f0794d1407e782b340d96e329389b04f.webp 1470w,https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/f0\\/794d1407e782b340d96e329389b04f\\/w1680\\/q80\\/wpojpg\\/images\\/uploads\\/f0794d1407e782b340d96e329389b04f.webp 1680w,https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/f0\\/794d1407e782b340d96e329389b04f\\/w1870\\/q80\\/wpojpg\\/images\\/uploads\\/f0794d1407e782b340d96e329389b04f.webp 1870w,https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/f0\\/794d1407e782b340d96e329389b04f\\/w2048\\/q80\\/wpojpg\\/images\\/uploads\\/f0794d1407e782b340d96e329389b04f.webp 2048w,https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/f0\\/794d1407e782b340d96e329389b04f\\/w2880\\/q80\\/wpojpg\\/images\\/uploads\\/f0794d1407e782b340d96e329389b04f.webp 2880w\\\"\",\"image_alt\":\"\",\"image_cap\":\"\",\"image_data\":[\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/f0\\/794d1407e782b340d96e329389b04f\\/w880\\/q80\\/wpojpg\\/images\\/uploads\\/f0794d1407e782b340d96e329389b04f.webp 880w\",\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/f0\\/794d1407e782b340d96e329389b04f\\/w1210\\/q80\\/wpojpg\\/images\\/uploads\\/f0794d1407e782b340d96e329389b04f.webp 1210w\",\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/f0\\/794d1407e782b340d96e329389b04f\\/w1470\\/q80\\/wpojpg\\/images\\/uploads\\/f0794d1407e782b340d96e329389b04f.webp 1470w\",\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/f0\\/794d1407e782b340d96e329389b04f\\/w1680\\/q80\\/wpojpg\\/images\\/uploads\\/f0794d1407e782b340d96e329389b04f.webp 1680w\",\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/f0\\/794d1407e782b340d96e329389b04f\\/w1870\\/q80\\/wpojpg\\/images\\/uploads\\/f0794d1407e782b340d96e329389b04f.webp 1870w\",\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/f0\\/794d1407e782b340d96e329389b04f\\/w2048\\/q80\\/wpojpg\\/images\\/uploads\\/f0794d1407e782b340d96e329389b04f.webp 2048w\",\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/f0\\/794d1407e782b340d96e329389b04f\\/w2880\\/q80\\/wpojpg\\/images\\/uploads\\/f0794d1407e782b340d96e329389b04f.webp 2880w\"],\"focal_point\":[\"48.0\",\"50.2\"],\"search_text\":\"Two people meet for a drink the night before a criminal trial that will change both their lives forever. First Last Dance\\u00a0is a new play about trust, sacrifice and why we\\u2019re so obsessed with romance when the world is on fire. The script was written on the Jerwood HighTide writers\\u00a0group and shortlisted for the 2026 VCA Playwriting Prize. This work in progress sharing is supported by the Peter Shaffer Foundation and Riverside Studios.\\u00a0Creatives:Aisling\\u00a0Towl is is a playwright and poet from South London. She is an alumnus of the Royal Court playwrights\\u2019 group and the Jerwood HighTide writers group, and has had work staged at venues including King's Head Theatre, Soho Theatre and Cambridge Guildhall. Her poetry has been shortlisted for the Bridpoint Prize, nominated for the Pushcart Prize and published in journals including\\u00a0Basket Magazine, And Other Poems and The Seaford Review.\\u00a0She was the 2024-25 Peter Shaffer Playwright in Residence at Trinity College, Cambridge, and is a 2026 Hawthornden Fellow.Harry Tennison is a theatre director and dramaturg from Harlow in Essex, now based in South London. Credits include: HighTide Rising (Soho Theatre and New Wolsey Theatre), The Beautiful Future is Coming (Jermyn Street Theatre), I Know I Know I Know (Southwark Playhouse), Robin Hood (The Maltings, Ely), Sleeping Beauty (The Grange, Hartford). He was previously a part of Mercury Theatre\\u2019s Directors Scheme. He co-runs new writing company DONOTALIGHT, a new theatre company interested in new writing about living in the world today. Their work is grounded in formal inventiveness and telling political stories through a personal lens.Folu Odimayo is a choreographer, performer and movement director whose practice focuses on finding articulation and poetry through movement. As a dancer, he has worked for a variety of companies and artists such as Punchdrunk\\u2019s The Burnt City, Holly Blakey, Bullyache amongst others. Experience as a choreographer stretches across music videos for artists such as Pem, Autoheart, Harvey Causon, gallery works at the Serpentine, as well as his own film work which has been featured on Director\\u2019s Notes and commissioned by Sadler\\u2019s Wells Theatre.\\u00a0\\u00a0Cast:Rosie Dwyer (F1: The Movie, The Beautiful Future is Coming, Sex Education)Simon Lennon (G'wed, Death in Paradise, Bridgerton)\",\"book_link\":\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/seats\\/255202\\/\",\"event_type\":[\"3\"],\"theatre\":[\"81013\"],\"search\":\"First Last Dance (A Riverside R&D Sharing) First Last Dance (A Riverside R&D Sharing) Theatre  <p>Two people meet for a drink the night before a criminal trial that will change both their lives forever. <i>First Last Dance<\\/i>&nbsp;is a new play about trust, sacrifice and why we\\u2019re so obsessed with romance when the world is on fire. The script was written on the Jerwood HighTide writers&nbsp;group and shortlisted for the 2026 VCA Playwriting Prize. This work in progress sharing is supported by the Peter Shaffer Foundation and Riverside Studios.<\\/p><p>&nbsp;<\\/p><p>Creatives:<\\/p><p><i><strong>Aisling&nbsp;Towl <\\/strong><\\/i>is is a playwright and poet from South London. She is an alumnus of the Royal Court playwrights\\u2019 group and the Jerwood HighTide writers group, and has had work staged at venues including King's Head Theatre, Soho Theatre and Cambridge Guildhall. Her poetry has been shortlisted for the Bridpoint Prize, nominated for the Pushcart Prize and published in journals including<i>&nbsp;Basket Magazine, And Other Poems and The Seaford Review.<\\/i>&nbsp;She was the 2024-25 Peter Shaffer Playwright in Residence at Trinity College, Cambridge, and is a 2026 Hawthornden Fellow.<\\/p><p><i><strong>Harry Tennison<\\/strong><\\/i> is a theatre director and dramaturg from Harlow in Essex, now based in South London. Credits include: <i>HighTide Rising<\\/i> (Soho Theatre and New Wolsey Theatre), <i>The Beautiful Future is Coming<\\/i> (Jermyn Street Theatre), <i>I Know I Know I Know<\\/i> (Southwark Playhouse), <i>Robin Hood<\\/i> (The Maltings, Ely), <i>Sleeping Beauty <\\/i>(The Grange, Hartford). He was previously a part of Mercury Theatre\\u2019s Directors Scheme. He co-runs new writing company DONOTALIGHT, a new theatre company interested in new writing about living in the world today. Their work is grounded in formal inventiveness and telling political stories through a personal lens.<\\/p><p><i><strong>Folu Odimayo <\\/strong><\\/i>is a choreographer, performer and movement director whose practice focuses on finding articulation and poetry through movement. As a dancer, he has worked for a variety of companies and artists such as Punchdrunk\\u2019s <i>The Burnt City<\\/i>, <i>Holly Blakey<\\/i>, <i>Bullyache <\\/i>amongst others. Experience as a choreographer stretches across music videos for artists such as Pem, Autoheart, Harvey Causon, gallery works at the Serpentine, as well as his own film work which has been featured on Director\\u2019s Notes and commissioned by Sadler\\u2019s Wells Theatre.&nbsp;<\\/p><p>&nbsp;<\\/p><p>Cast:<\\/p><p><strong>Rosie Dwyer <\\/strong>(<i>F1: The Movie<\\/i>, <i>The Beautiful Future is Coming<\\/i>, <i>Sex Education<\\/i>)<\\/p><p><strong>Simon Lennon<\\/strong> (<i>G'wed<\\/i>, <i>Death in Paradise<\\/i>, <i>Bridgerton<\\/i>)<\\/p> First Last Dance (A Riverside R&D Sharing)  Two people meet for a drink the night before a criminal trial that will change both their lives forever. First Last Dance\\u00a0is a new play about trust, sacrifice and why we\\u2019re so obsessed with romance when the world is on fire. The script was written on the Jerwood HighTide writers\\u00a0group and shortlisted for the 2026 VCA Playwriting Prize. This work in progress sharing is supported by the Peter Shaffer Foundation and Riverside Studios.\\u00a0Creatives:Aisling\\u00a0Towl is is a playwright and poet from South London. She is an alumnus of the Royal Court playwrights\\u2019 group and the Jerwood HighTide writers group, and has had work staged at venues including King's Head Theatre, Soho Theatre and Cambridge Guildhall. Her poetry has been shortlisted for the Bridpoint Prize, nominated for the Pushcart Prize and published in journals including\\u00a0Basket Magazine, And Other Poems and The Seaford Review.\\u00a0She was the 2024-25 Peter Shaffer Playwright in Residence at Trinity College, Cambridge, and is a 2026 Hawthornden Fellow.Harry Tennison is a theatre director and dramaturg from Harlow in Essex, now based in South London. Credits include: HighTide Rising (Soho Theatre and New Wolsey Theatre), The Beautiful Future is Coming (Jermyn Street Theatre), I Know I Know I Know (Southwark Playhouse), Robin Hood (The Maltings, Ely), Sleeping Beauty (The Grange, Hartford). He was previously a part of Mercury Theatre\\u2019s Directors Scheme. He co-runs new writing company DONOTALIGHT, a new theatre company interested in new writing about living in the world today. Their work is grounded in formal inventiveness and telling political stories through a personal lens.Folu Odimayo is a choreographer, performer and movement director whose practice focuses on finding articulation and poetry through movement. As a dancer, he has worked for a variety of companies and artists such as Punchdrunk\\u2019s The Burnt City, Holly Blakey, Bullyache amongst others. Experience as a choreographer stretches across music videos for artists such as Pem, Autoheart, Harvey Causon, gallery works at the Serpentine, as well as his own film work which has been featured on Director\\u2019s Notes and commissioned by Sadler\\u2019s Wells Theatre.\\u00a0\\u00a0Cast:Rosie Dwyer (F1: The Movie, The Beautiful Future is Coming, Sex Education)Simon Lennon (G'wed, Death in Paradise, Bridgerton) Theatre Riverside R&D\"},{\"url\":\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/whats-on\\/uuc-the-odyssey\\/\",\"id\":\"3913\",\"name\":\"The Odyssey\",\"title\":\"The Odyssey\",\"duration\":\"172 minutes\",\"slot_tag\":\"Cinema\",\"link_title\":\"More Info\",\"performances\":{\"1784242800\":[{\"tag_ids\":[\"101\",\"81000\",\"80879\"],\"tag_name\":\"\",\"html\":\"<a class=\\\"performance button\\\" href=\\\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/seats\\/247802\\/\\\">\\n   \\n      <div class=\\\"performance-time\\\" data-acc=\\\"\\\">16:30<\\/div>\\n    \\n<\\/a>\\n\",\"timestamp\":\"1784302200\",\"accessibility_class\":\"\"},{\"tag_ids\":[\"101\",\"81000\",\"80879\"],\"tag_name\":\"\",\"html\":\"<a class=\\\"performance button\\\" href=\\\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/seats\\/249001\\/\\\">\\n   \\n      <div class=\\\"performance-time\\\" data-acc=\\\"\\\">17:15<\\/div>\\n    \\n<\\/a>\\n\",\"timestamp\":\"1784304900\",\"accessibility_class\":\"\"},{\"tag_ids\":[\"101\",\"81000\",\"80879\"],\"tag_name\":\"\",\"html\":\"<a class=\\\"performance button\\\" href=\\\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/seats\\/248001\\/\\\">\\n   \\n      <div class=\\\"performance-time\\\" data-acc=\\\"\\\">20:00<\\/div>\\n    \\n<\\/a>\\n\",\"timestamp\":\"1784314800\",\"accessibility_class\":\"\"}],\"1784329200\":[{\"tag_ids\":[\"101\",\"81000\",\"80879\"],\"tag_name\":\"\",\"html\":\"<a class=\\\"performance button\\\" href=\\\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/seats\\/248201\\/\\\">\\n   \\n      <div class=\\\"performance-time\\\" data-acc=\\\"\\\">10:00<\\/div>\\n    \\n<\\/a>\\n\",\"timestamp\":\"1784365200\",\"accessibility_class\":\"\"},{\"tag_ids\":[\"101\",\"81000\",\"80879\"],\"tag_name\":\"\",\"html\":\"<a class=\\\"performance button\\\" href=\\\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\