homas Hayslip.Age Rating:12ALanguage:EnglishContent Warnings:Strong violenceDirector:Christopher NolanCast:Matt Damon, Tom Holland, Anne Hathaway, Robert Pattinson and Lupita Nyong\\u2019o, with Zendaya and Charlize TheronCompany:UniversalInterval:NoneTrailers:20 minsYear of Release:2026Audio Described:Yes\",\"book_link\":false,\"accessibility\":[\"80879\"],\"event_age_ratings\":[\"81000\"],\"event_type\":[\"101\"],\"search\":\"The Odyssey The Odyssey Cinema  <p>Christopher Nolan\\u2019s next film, <i><strong>The Odyssey<\\/strong><\\/i>, is a mythic action epic shot across the world using brand new IMAX\\u00ae film technology. The film brings Homer\\u2019s foundational saga to IMAX\\u00ae film screens for the first time and opens in cinemas everywhere on July 17, 2026. &nbsp;<\\/p><p><i>The Odyssey <\\/i>is produced by Emma Thomas and Christopher Nolan for their company, Syncopy. The executive producer is Thomas Hayslip.<\\/p><figure class=\\\"table\\\"><table><tbody><tr><td><strong>Age Rating:<\\/strong><\\/td><td>12A<\\/td><\\/tr><tr><td><strong>Language:<\\/strong><\\/td><td>English<\\/td><\\/tr><tr><td><strong>Content Warnings:<\\/strong><\\/td><td>Strong violence<\\/td><\\/tr><tr><td><strong>Director:<\\/strong><\\/td><td>Christopher Nolan<\\/td><\\/tr><tr><td><strong>Cast:<\\/strong><\\/td><td>Matt Damon, Tom Holland, Anne Hathaway, Robert Pattinson and Lupita Nyong\\u2019o, with Zendaya and Charlize Theron<\\/td><\\/tr><tr><td><strong>Company:<\\/strong><\\/td><td>Universal<\\/td><\\/tr><tr><td><strong>Interval:<\\/strong><\\/td><td>None<\\/td><\\/tr><tr><td><strong>Trailers:<\\/strong><\\/td><td>20 mins<\\/td><\\/tr><tr><td><strong>Year of Release:<\\/strong><\\/td><td>2026<\\/td><\\/tr><tr><td><strong>Audio Described:<\\/strong><\\/td><td>Yes<\\/td><\\/tr><\\/tbody><\\/table><\\/figure> The Odyssey  Christopher Nolan\\u2019s next film, The Odyssey, is a mythic action epic shot across the world using brand new IMAX\\u00ae film technology. The film brings Homer\\u2019s foundational saga to IMAX\\u00ae film screens for the first time and opens in cinemas everywhere on July 17, 2026. \\u00a0The Odyssey is produced by Emma Thomas and Christopher Nolan for their company, Syncopy. The executive producer is Thomas Hayslip.Age Rating:12ALanguage:EnglishContent Warnings:Strong violenceDirector:Christopher NolanCast:Matt Damon, Tom Holland, Anne Hathaway, Robert Pattinson and Lupita Nyong\\u2019o, with Zendaya and Charlize TheronCompany:UniversalInterval:NoneTrailers:20 minsYear of Release:2026Audio Described:Yes Audio Described 15 Cinema\"},{\"url\":\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/whats-on\\/Xl-redrafting-with-beth-flintoff\\/\",\"id\":\"3208\",\"name\":\"Redrafting with Beth Flintoff\",\"title\":\"Redrafting with Beth Flintoff\",\"duration\":\"180 minutes\",\"slot_tag\":\"Workshops & Classes\",\"link_title\":\"More Info\",\"performances\":{\"1784329200\":[{\"tag_ids\":[\"72\",\"81015\"],\"tag_name\":\"\",\"html\":\"<a class=\\\"performance button\\\" href=\\\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/seats\\/263201\\/\\\">\\n   \\n      <div class=\\\"performance-time\\\" data-acc=\\\"\\\">10:30<\\/div>\\n    \\n<\\/a>\\n\",\"timestamp\":\"1784367000\",\"accessibility_class\":\"\"}]},\"performance_dates\":[1784329200],\"times\":[1784367000],\"start_date\":\"1784367000\",\"end_date\":\"1784367000\",\"age_rating_class\":\"\",\"ticket_free\":false,\"priority_booking\":true,\"hash\":\"M1ZsTEhFTlVqcGM2eVRNaUZBbGFOQT09\",\"embed_id\":\"\",\"embed_host\":\"\",\"date_formatted\":\"Sat 18 Jul 2026\",\"text\":\"Welcome to SCRUM\\u2019s summer writing workshop series! You can explore the full programme here: https:\\/\\/www.scrumtheatre.co.uk\\/current-workshops&nbsp;SCRUM&hellip;\",\"image_url\":\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/7a\\/0a8b7bb1e863de77564b7ba45e8cbc\\/w880\\/q80\\/cx1145\\/cy13\\/cw1862\\/ch1862\\/images\\/uploads\\/7a0a8b7bb1e863de77564b7ba45e8cbc.png\",\"image_source\":\"type=\\\"image\\/webp\\\" srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/7a\\/0a8b7bb1e863de77564b7ba45e8cbc\\/w880\\/q80\\/wpopng\\/cx1145\\/cy13\\/cw1862\\/ch1862\\/images\\/uploads\\/7a0a8b7bb1e863de77564b7ba45e8cbc.webp 880w,https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/7a\\/0a8b7bb1e863de77564b7ba45e8cbc\\/w1210\\/q80\\/wpopng\\/cx1145\\/cy13\\/cw1862\\/ch1862\\/images\\/uploads\\/7a0a8b7bb1e863de77564b7ba45e8cbc.webp 1210w,https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/7a\\/0a8b7bb1e863de77564b7ba45e8cbc\\/w1470\\/q80\\/wpopng\\/cx1145\\/cy13\\/cw1862\\/ch1862\\/images\\/uploads\\/7a0a8b7bb1e863de77564b7ba45e8cbc.webp 1470w,https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/7a\\/0a8b7bb1e863de77564b7ba45e8cbc\\/w1680\\/q80\\/wpopng\\/cx1145\\/cy13\\/cw1862\\/ch1862\\/images\\/uploads\\/7a0a8b7bb1e863de77564b7ba45e8cbc.webp 1680w,https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/7a\\/0a8b7bb1e863de77564b7ba45e8cbc\\/w1870\\/q80\\/wpopng\\/cx1145\\/cy13\\/cw1862\\/ch1862\\/images\\/uploads\\/7a0a8b7bb1e863de77564b7ba45e8cbc.webp 1870w,https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/7a\\/0a8b7bb1e863de77564b7ba45e8cbc\\/w2048\\/q80\\/wpopng\\/cx1145\\/cy13\\/cw1862\\/ch1862\\/images\\/uploads\\/7a0a8b7bb1e863de77564b7ba45e8cbc.webp 2048w,https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/7a\\/0a8b7bb1e863de77564b7ba45e8cbc\\/w2880\\/q80\\/wpopng\\/cx1145\\/cy13\\/cw1862\\/ch1862\\/images\\/uploads\\/7a0a8b7bb1e863de77564b7ba45e8cbc.webp 2880w\\\"\",\"image_alt\":\"\",\"image_cap\":\"\",\"image_data\":[\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/7a\\/0a8b7bb1e863de77564b7ba45e8cbc\\/w880\\/q80\\/wpopng\\/cx1145\\/cy13\\/cw1862\\/ch1862\\/images\\/uploads\\/7a0a8b7bb1e863de77564b7ba45e8cbc.webp 880w\",\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/7a\\/0a8b7bb1e863de77564b7ba45e8cbc\\/w1210\\/q80\\/wpopng\\/cx1145\\/cy13\\/cw1862\\/ch1862\\/images\\/uploads\\/7a0a8b7bb1e863de77564b7ba45e8cbc.webp 1210w\",\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/7a\\/0a8b7bb1e863de77564b7ba45e8cbc\\/w1470\\/q80\\/wpopng\\/cx1145\\/cy13\\/cw1862\\/ch1862\\/images\\/uploads\\/7a0a8b7bb1e863de77564b7ba45e8cbc.webp 1470w\",\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/7a\\/0a8b7bb1e863de77564b7ba45e8cbc\\/w1680\\/q80\\/wpopng\\/cx1145\\/cy13\\/cw1862\\/ch1862\\/images\\/uploads\\/7a0a8b7bb1e863de77564b7ba45e8cbc.webp 1680w\",\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/7a\\/0a8b7bb1e863de77564b7ba45e8cbc\\/w1870\\/q80\\/wpopng\\/cx1145\\/cy13\\/cw1862\\/ch1862\\/images\\/uploads\\/7a0a8b7bb1e863de77564b7ba45e8cbc.webp 1870w\",\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/7a\\/0a8b7bb1e863de77564b7ba45e8cbc\\/w2048\\/q80\\/wpopng\\/cx1145\\/cy13\\/cw1862\\/ch1862\\/images\\/uploads\\/7a0a8b7bb1e863de77564b7ba45e8cbc.webp 2048w\",\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/7a\\/0a8b7bb1e863de77564b7ba45e8cbc\\/w2880\\/q80\\/wpopng\\/cx1145\\/cy13\\/cw1862\\/ch1862\\/images\\/uploads\\/7a0a8b7bb1e863de77564b7ba45e8cbc.webp 2880w\"],\"focal_point\":[\"50\",\"50\"],\"search_text\":\"Welcome to SCRUM\\u2019s summer writing workshop series! You can explore the full programme here: https:\\/\\/www.scrumtheatre.co.uk\\/current-workshops\\u00a0SCRUM offers tiered pricing for our workshops - please read the pricing information below to choose the right tier for you.\\u00a0After the workshop with Beth Flintoff we invite you to join us for Snacks \\u2018n\\u2019 Chats! We're holding tea for all workshop attendees from 1-2pm - a chance to get to know your fellow creatives, skill swap and, most importantly, eat biscuits.\\u00a0Redrafting with Beth FlintoffCongratulations! You\\u2019ve written a play (or most of it?) - an amazing achievement! Now what? Beth will take you through the process of honing and reworking your script, taking a fresh look at what your play is really about, and giving you tools to get the feedback you really need. This will be a supportive, practical workshop, with some time for writing, exercises and discussion, so please bring a project you are already working on.Beth Flintoff is a playwright, dramaturg, and theatre-maker. She is an Associate Playwright at the Royal Court Theatre in London and an Associate Artist at RABBLE in Reading. Her published plays The Glove Thief, Rebellious Women and The Ballad of Maria Marten are regularly performed around the world. The Ballad of Maria Marten\\u00a0has toured the UK three times, been translated into several languages, and in 2024 it was NHB\\u2019s second most frequently performed play around the world.\\u00a0\\u00a0WHICH TICKET TIER SHOULD I CHOOSE?Offering affordable training is at the heart of SCRUM\\u2019s charitable objectives, which is why we have different ticket price tiers. We encourage you to pay what you can based on the below descriptors:\\u00a312 - Subsidised ticket price\\u00a0- You have limited expendable income** and need to opt for the lowest cost option. If this cost is still a barrier, please contact SCRUM on workshops@scrumtheatre.co.uk\\u00a315 - Subsidised ticket price - You have some expendable income and can meet basic needs, even if there may be occasional financial stress\\u00a320 - Full ticket price\\u00a0- You have a comfortable amount of expendable income, do not face financial barriers and are able to cover the full cost of the event ticket.\\u00a0*BASIC NEEDS include food, housing, clothing and transportation.**EXPENDABLE INCOME might mean you are able to buy coffee or tea at a shop, go to the cinema or a concert, buy new clothes, books and similar items each month, etc.\\u00a0Want to hear about the latest SCRUM workshops and more? Join the SCRUM mailing list here. www.scrumtheatre.co.uk\",\"book_link\":\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/seats\\/263201\\/\",\"event_type\":[\"72\"],\"theatre\":[\"81015\"],\"search\":\"Redrafting with Beth Flintoff Redrafting with Beth Flintoff Workshops & Classes  <p>Welcome to SCRUM\\u2019s summer writing workshop series! You can explore the full programme here: <a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.scrumtheatre.co.uk\\/current-workshops\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\">https:\\/\\/www.scrumtheatre.co.uk\\/current-workshops&nbsp;<\\/a><\\/p><p>SCRUM offers tiered pricing for our workshops - please read the pricing information below to choose the right tier for you.&nbsp;<\\/p><p>After the workshop with Beth Flintoff we invite you to join us for <i>Snacks \\u2018n\\u2019 Chats<\\/i>! We're holding tea for all workshop attendees from 1-2pm - a chance to get to know your fellow creatives, skill swap and, most importantly, eat biscuits.<\\/p><p>&nbsp;<\\/p><p><strong>Redrafting with Beth Flintoff<\\/strong><\\/p><p>Congratulations! You\\u2019ve written a play (or most of it?) - an amazing achievement! Now what? Beth will take you through the process of honing and reworking your script, taking a fresh look at what your play is really about, and giving you tools to get the feedback you really need. This will be a supportive, practical workshop, with some time for writing, exercises and discussion, so please bring a project you are already working on.<\\/p><p>Beth Flintoff is a playwright, dramaturg, and theatre-maker. She is an Associate Playwright at the Royal Court Theatre in London and an Associate Artist at RABBLE in Reading. Her published plays <i>The Glove Thief, Rebellious Women <\\/i>and <i>The Ballad of Maria Marten <\\/i>are regularly performed around the world. <i>The Ballad of Maria Marten<\\/i>&nbsp;has toured the UK three times, been translated into several languages, and in 2024 it was NHB\\u2019s second most frequently performed play around the world.&nbsp;<\\/p><p>&nbsp;<\\/p><p><strong>WHICH TICKET TIER SHOULD I CHOOSE?<\\/strong><\\/p><p>Offering affordable training is at the heart of SCRUM\\u2019s charitable objectives, which is why we have different ticket price tiers. We encourage you to pay what you can based on the below descriptors:<\\/p><p>\\u00a312 - <i>Subsidised ticket price<\\/i>&nbsp;- You have limited expendable income** and need to opt for the lowest cost option. If this cost is still a barrier, please contact SCRUM on <a href=\\\"mailto:workshops@scrumtheatre.co.uk\\\">workshops@scrumtheatre.co.uk<\\/a><\\/p><p>\\u00a315 - <i>Subsidised ticket price <\\/i>- You have some expendable income and can meet basic needs, even if there may be occasional financial stress<\\/p><p>\\u00a320 - <i>Full ticket price<\\/i>&nbsp;- You have a comfortable amount of expendable income, do not face financial barriers and are able to cover the full cost of the event ticket.&nbsp;<\\/p><p>*BASIC NEEDS include food, housing, clothing and transportation.<\\/p><p>**EXPENDABLE INCOME might mean you are able to buy coffee or tea at a shop, go to the cinema or a concert, buy new clothes, books and similar items each month, etc.<\\/p><p>&nbsp;<\\/p><p>Want to hear about the latest SCRUM workshops and more? Join the SCRUM mailing list here. <a href=\\\"http:\\/\\/www.scrumtheatre.co.uk\\/\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\">www.scrumtheatre.co.uk<\\/a><\\/p> Redrafting with Beth Flintoff  Welcome to SCRUM\\u2019s summer writing workshop series! You can explore the full programme here: https:\\/\\/www.scrumtheatre.co.uk\\/current-workshops\\u00a0SCRUM offers tiered pricing for our workshops - please read the pricing information below to choose the right tier for you.\\u00a0After the workshop with Beth Flintoff we invite you to join us for Snacks \\u2018n\\u2019 Chats! We're holding tea for all workshop attendees from 1-2pm - a chance to get to know your fellow creatives, skill swap and, most importantly, eat biscuits.\\u00a0Redrafting with Beth FlintoffCongratulations! You\\u2019ve written a play (or most of it?) - an amazing achievement! Now what? Beth will take you through the process of honing and reworking your script, taking a fresh look at what your play is really about, and giving you tools to get the feedback you really need. This will be a supportive, practical workshop, with some time for writing, exercises and discussion, so please bring a project you are already working on.Beth Flintoff is a playwright, dramaturg, and theatre-maker. She is an Associate Playwright at the Royal Court Theatre in London and an Associate Artist at RABBLE in Reading. Her published plays The Glove Thief, Rebellious Women and The Ballad of Maria Marten are regularly performed around the world. The Ballad of Maria Marten\\u00a0has toured the UK three times, been translated into several languages, and in 2024 it was NHB\\u2019s second most frequently performed play around the world.\\u00a0\\u00a0WHICH TICKET TIER SHOULD I CHOOSE?Offering affordable training is at the heart of SCRUM\\u2019s charitable objectives, which is why we have different ticket price tiers. We encourage you to pay what you can based on the below descriptors:\\u00a312 - Subsidised ticket price\\u00a0- You have limited expendable income** and need to opt for the lowest cost option. If this cost is still a barrier, please contact SCRUM on workshops@scrumtheatre.co.uk\\u00a315 - Subsidised ticket price - You have some expendable income and can meet basic needs, even if there may be occasional financial stress\\u00a320 - Full ticket price\\u00a0- You have a comfortable amount of expendable income, do not face financial barriers and are able to cover the full cost of the event ticket.\\u00a0*BASIC NEEDS include food, housing, clothing and transportation.**EXPENDABLE INCOME might mean you are able to buy coffee or tea at a shop, go to the cinema or a concert, buy new clothes, books and similar items each month, etc.\\u00a0Want to hear about the latest SCRUM workshops and more? Join the SCRUM mailing list here. www.scrumtheatre.co.uk Workshops & Classes SCRUM Theatre\"},{\"url\":\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/whats-on\\/uPI-clash-of-the-titans\\/\",\"id\":\"4066\",\"name\":\"Clash of the Titans\",\"title\":\"Clash of the Titans\",\"duration\":\"118 minutes\",\"slot_tag\":\"Cinema\",\"link_title\":\"More Info\",\"performances\":{\"1784329200\":[{\"tag_ids\":[\"101\",\"80998\",\"81024\"],\"tag_name\":\"\",\"html\":\"<a class=\\\"performance button\\\" href=\\\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/seats\\/255401\\/\\\">\\n   \\n      <div class=\\\"performance-time\\\" data-acc=\\\"\\\">14:00<\\/div>\\n    \\n<\\/a>\\n\",\"timestamp\":\"1784379600\",\"accessibility_class\":\"\"}],\"1784415600\":[{\"tag_ids\":[\"101\",\"80998\",\"81024\"],\"tag_name\":\"\",\"html\":\"<a class=\\\"performance button\\\" href=\\\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/seats\\/255601\\/\\\">\\n   \\n      <div class=\\\"performance-time\\\" data-acc=\\\"\\\">14:30<\\/div>\\n    \\n<\\/a>\\n\",\"timestamp\":\"1784467800\",\"accessibility_class\":\"\"}],\"1784502000\":[{\"tag_ids\":[\"101\",\"80998\",\"81024\",\"80787\"],\"tag_name\":\"\",\"html\":\"<a class=\\\"performance button\\\" href=\\\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/seats\\/255801\\/\\\">\\n   \\n      <div class=\\\"performance-time\\\" data-acc=\\\"\\\">11:30<\\/div>\\n    \\n<\\/a>\\n    <div class=\\\"tooltip\\\" data-tooltip_theme=\\\"#00782A\\\" data-tooltip_text=\\\"Our special screenings for over 60s during quieter times of the day, where we show a selection of new, talk-of-the-town releases and timeless classics. The price includes a complimentary hot drink and biscuits, served before the film.\\\">Silver Screen<\\/div>\\n\",\"timestamp\":\"1784543400\",\"accessibility_class\":\"\"}]},\"performance_dates\":[1784329200,1784415600,1784502000],\"times\":[1784379600,1784467800,1784543400],\"start_date\":\"1784379600\",\"end_date\":\"1784543400\",\"age_rating_class\":\"18\",\"ticket_free\":false,\"priority_booking\":true,\"hash\":\"Q0tkc3poREg3ckpJMURDZ0Z6SVN6dz09\",\"embed_id\":\"\",\"embed_host\":\"\",\"date_formatted\":\"Sat 18 - Mon 20 Jul 2026\",\"text\":\"As master filmmaker Christopher Nolan finally reveals his ambitious take on Homer's epic THE ODYSSEY this July, travel back with us through the ages to&hellip;\",\"image_url\":\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/39\\/6538bc931dd398ffa897aeb8b06c7e\\/w880\\/q80\\/cx19\\/cw1263\\/ch1266\\/images\\/uploads\\/396538bc931dd398ffa897aeb8b06c7e.png\",\"image_source\":\"type=\\\"image\\/webp\\\" srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/39\\/6538bc931dd398ffa897aeb8b06c7e\\/w880\\/q80\\/wpopng\\/cx19\\/cw1263\\/ch1266\\/images\\/uploads\\/396538bc931dd398ffa897aeb8b06c7e.webp 880w,https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/39\\/6538bc931dd398ffa897aeb8b06c7e\\/w1210\\/q80\\/wpopng\\/cx19\\/cw1263\\/ch1266\\/images\\/uploads\\/396538bc931dd398ffa897aeb8b06c7e.webp 1210w,https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/39\\/6538bc931dd398ffa897aeb8b06c7e\\/w1470\\/q80\\/wpopng\\/cx19\\/cw1263\\/ch1266\\/images\\/uploads\\/396538bc931dd398ffa897aeb8b06c7e.webp 1470w,https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/39\\/6538bc931dd398ffa897aeb8b06c7e\\/w1680\\/q80\\/wpopng\\/cx19\\/cw1263\\/ch1266\\/images\\/uploads\\/396538bc931dd398ffa897aeb8b06c7e.webp 1680w,https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/39\\/6538bc931dd398ffa897aeb8b06c7e\\/w1870\\/q80\\/wpopng\\/cx19\\/cw1263\\/ch1266\\/images\\/uploads\\/396538bc931dd398ffa897aeb8b06c7e.webp 1870w,https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/39\\/6538bc931dd398ffa897aeb8b06c7e\\/w1920\\/q80\\/wpopng\\/cx19\\/cw1263\\/ch1266\\/images\\/uploads\\/396538bc931dd398ffa897aeb8b06c7e.webp 2048w,https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/39\\/6538bc931dd398ffa897aeb8b06c7e\\/w1920\\/q80\\/wpopng\\/cx19\\/cw1263\\/ch1266\\/images\\/uploads\\/396538bc931dd398ffa897aeb8b06c7e.webp 2880w\\\"\",\"image_alt\":\"\",\"image_cap\":\"\",\"image_data\":[\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/39\\/6538bc931dd398ffa897aeb8b06c7e\\/w880\\/q80\\/wpopng\\/cx19\\/cw1263\\/ch1266\\/images\\/uploads\\/396538bc931dd398ffa897aeb8b06c7e.webp 880w\",\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/39\\/6538bc931dd398ffa897aeb8b06c7e\\/w1210\\/q80\\/wpopng\\/cx19\\/cw1263\\/ch1266\\/images\\/uploads\\/396538bc931dd398ffa897aeb8b06c7e.webp 1210w\",\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/39\\/6538bc931dd398ffa897aeb8b06c7e\\/w1470\\/q80\\/wpopng\\/cx19\\/cw1263\\/ch1266\\/images\\/uploads\\/396538bc931dd398ffa897aeb8b06c7e.webp 1470w\",\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/39\\/6538bc931dd398ffa897aeb8b06c7e\\/w1680\\/q80\\/wpopng\\/cx19\\/cw1263\\/ch1266\\/images\\/uploads\\/396538bc931dd398ffa897aeb8b06c7e.webp 1680w\",\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/39\\/6538bc931dd398ffa897aeb8b06c7e\\/w1870\\/q80\\/wpopng\\/cx19\\/cw1263\\/ch1266\\/images\\/uploads\\/396538bc931dd398ffa897aeb8b06c7e.webp 1870w\",\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/39\\/6538bc931dd398ffa897aeb8b06c7e\\/w1920\\/q80\\/wpopng\\/cx19\\/cw1263\\/ch1266\\/images\\/uploads\\/396538bc931dd398ffa897aeb8b06c7e.webp 2048w\",\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/39\\/6538bc931dd398ffa897aeb8b06c7e\\/w1920\\/q80\\/wpopng\\/cx19\\/cw1263\\/ch1266\\/images\\/uploads\\/396538bc931dd398ffa897aeb8b06c7e.webp 2880w\"],\"focal_point\":[\"47.6\",\"26.0\"],\"search_text\":\"As master filmmaker Christopher Nolan finally reveals his ambitious take on Homer's epic THE ODYSSEY this July, travel back with us through the ages to explore how other filmmakers have drawn on the ancient myths of yesterday to forge groundbreaking big screen entertainment. Enjoy a multi-buy offer for all films in the MYTHS AND MONSTERS season with 15% off adult and concession prices if more than one ticket is purchased in same order.\\u00a0MYTHS AND MONSTERS classic film season at Riverside Studios:Clash of the Titans (1981): 18th-20th JulySpartacus (1960): 25-28th JulyTroy (2004): 1st-3rd August\\u00a0CLASH OF THE TITANS (1981)The machinations of gods above and the fates of man and monsters here below play out in 1981's Clash of the Titans. Decades prior to the sensational 2010 version of the tale, Harry Hamlin took up sword and shield to play valorous Perseus, mortal son of Zeus (Laurence Olivier) who sets out to fulfill his destiny by rescuing beloved Andromeda from the wrath of goddess Thetis (Maggie Smith).Perils await Perseus time and again. And eye-filling thrills await viewers as stop-motion effects legend Ray Harryhausen unleashes snake-haired Medusa, fearsome Kraken, winged Pegasus, two-headed dog Dioskilos, giant scorpions and more!Age Rating:18Language:EnglishContent Warnings:TBCDirector:Desmond DavisCast:Laurence Olivier, Maggie Smith, Harry Hamlin, Judi Bowker, Ursula Andress, Burgess MeredithCompany:Park CircusTrailers:20 minsYear of Release:1981\",\"book_link\":false,\"event_age_ratings\":[\"80998\"],\"cinema\":[\"81024\"],\"event_type\":[\"101\"],\"search\":\"Clash of the Titans Clash of the Titans Cinema  <p>As master filmmaker Christopher Nolan finally reveals his ambitious take on Homer's epic <i>THE ODYSSEY<\\/i> this July, travel back with us through the ages to explore how other filmmakers have drawn on the ancient myths of yesterday to forge groundbreaking big screen entertainment. Enjoy a multi-buy offer for all films in the <strong>MYTHS AND MONSTERS<\\/strong> season with 15% off adult and concession prices if more than one ticket is purchased in same order.<\\/p><p>&nbsp;<\\/p><p><strong>MYTHS AND MONSTERS <\\/strong>classic film season at Riverside Studios:<\\/p><p><i>Clash of the Titans<\\/i> (1981): 18th-20th July<\\/p><p><i>Spartacus<\\/i> (1960): 25-28th July<\\/p><p><i>Troy <\\/i>(2004): 1st-3rd August<\\/p><p>&nbsp;<\\/p><p><i><strong>CLASH OF THE TITANS<\\/strong><\\/i><strong> (1981)<\\/strong><\\/p><p>The machinations of gods above and the fates of man and monsters here below play out in 1981's <i><strong>Clash of the Titans<\\/strong><\\/i>. Decades prior to the sensational 2010 version of the tale, Harry Hamlin took up sword and shield to play valorous Perseus, mortal son of Zeus (Laurence Olivier) who sets out to fulfill his destiny by rescuing beloved Andromeda from the wrath of goddess Thetis (Maggie Smith).<\\/p><p>Perils await Perseus time and again. And eye-filling thrills await viewers as stop-motion effects legend Ray Harryhausen unleashes snake-haired Medusa, fearsome Kraken, winged Pegasus, two-headed dog Dioskilos, giant scorpions and more!<\\/p><figure class=\\\"table\\\"><table><tbody><tr><td><strong>Age Rating:<\\/strong><\\/td><td>18<\\/td><\\/tr><tr><td><strong>Language:<\\/strong><\\/td><td>English<\\/td><\\/tr><tr><td><strong>Content Warnings:<\\/strong><\\/td><td>TBC<\\/td><\\/tr><tr><td><strong>Director:<\\/strong><\\/td><td>Desmond Davis<\\/td><\\/tr><tr><td><strong>Cast:<\\/strong><\\/td><td>Laurence Olivier, Maggie Smith, Harry Hamlin, Judi Bowker, Ursula Andress, Burgess Meredith<\\/td><\\/tr><tr><td><strong>Company:<\\/strong><\\/td><td>Park Circus<\\/td><\\/tr><tr><td><strong>Trailers:<\\/strong><\\/td><td>20 mins<\\/td><\\/tr><tr><td><strong>Year of Release:<\\/strong><\\/td><td>1981<\\/td><\\/tr><\\/tbody><\\/table><\\/figure> Clash of the Titans  As master filmmaker Christopher Nolan finally reveals his ambitious take on Homer's epic THE ODYSSEY this July, travel back with us through the ages to explore how other filmmakers have drawn on the ancient myths of yesterday to forge groundbreaking big screen entertainment. Enjoy a multi-buy offer for all films in the MYTHS AND MONSTERS season with 15% off adult and concession prices if more than one ticket is purchased in same order.\\u00a0MYTHS AND MONSTERS classic film season at Riverside Studios:Clash of the Titans (1981): 18th-20th JulySpartacus (1960): 25-28th JulyTroy (2004): 1st-3rd August\\u00a0CLASH OF THE TITANS (1981)The machinations of gods above and the fates of man and monsters here below play out in 1981's Clash of the Titans. Decades prior to the sensational 2010 version of the tale, Harry Hamlin took up sword and shield to play valorous Perseus, mortal son of Zeus (Laurence Olivier) who sets out to fulfill his destiny by rescuing beloved Andromeda from the wrath of goddess Thetis (Maggie Smith).Perils await Perseus time and again. And eye-filling thrills await viewers as stop-motion effects legend Ray Harryhausen unleashes snake-haired Medusa, fearsome Kraken, winged Pegasus, two-headed dog Dioskilos, giant scorpions and more!Age Rating:18Language:EnglishContent Warnings:TBCDirector:Desmond DavisCast:Laurence Olivier, Maggie Smith, Harry Hamlin, Judi Bowker, Ursula Andress, Burgess MeredithCompany:Park CircusTrailers:20 minsYear of Release:1981 18 Myths and Monsters Cinema\"},{\"url\":\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/whats-on\\/i9-riverside-writers-group-showcase-2026\\/\",\"id\":\"2804\",\"name\":\"Riverside Writers Group Showcase 2026\",\"title\":\"Riverside Writers Group Showcase 2026\",\"duration\":\"120 minutes\",\"slot_tag\":\"Theatre\",\"link_title\":\"More Info\",\"performances\":{\"1784329200\":[{\"tag_ids\":[\"3\"],\"tag_name\":\"\",\"html\":\"<a class=\\\"performance button\\\" href=\\\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/seats\\/179002\\/\\\">\\n   \\n      <div class=\\\"performance-time\\\" data-acc=\\\"\\\">19:00<\\/div>\\n    \\n<\\/a>\\n\",\"timestamp\":\"1784397600\",\"accessibility_class\":\"\"}],\"1784415600\":[{\"tag_ids\":[\"3\"],\"tag_name\":\"\",\"html\":\"<a class=\\\"performance button\\\" href=\\\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/seats\\/179003\\/\\\">\\n   \\n      <div class=\\\"performance-time\\\" data-acc=\\\"\\\">19:00<\\/div>\\n    \\n<\\/a>\\n\",\"timestamp\":\"1784484000\",\"accessibility_class\":\"\"}]},\"performance_dates\":[1784329200,1784415600],\"times\":[1784397600,1784484000],\"start_date\":\"1784397600\",\"end_date\":\"1784484000\",\"age_rating_class\":\"\",\"ticket_free\":false,\"priority_booking\":true,\"hash\":\"enpJR2pTOTB6OWk1YUYrb3lRNFhQQT09\",\"embed_id\":\"\",\"embed_host\":\"\",\"date_formatted\":\"Sat 18 - Sun 19 Jul 2026\",\"text\":\"The Riverside Writers Group is a five month writer's cohort launched at Riverside Studios in February 2026, led by actor, writer, and award winning facilitator&nbsp;Nadine&nbsp;Gray.The&hellip;\",\"image_url\":\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/44\\/e351dfc3086c55f90b596ddc345929\\/w880\\/q80\\/cx163\\/cy7\\/cw316\\/ch316\\/images\\/uploads\\/44e351dfc3086c55f90b596ddc345929.png\",\"image_source\":\"type=\\\"image\\/webp\\\" srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/44\\/e351dfc3086c55f90b596ddc345929\\/w518\\/q80\\/wpopng\\/cx163\\/cy7\\/cw316\\/ch316\\/images\\/uploads\\/44e351dfc3086c55f90b596ddc345929.webp 880w,https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/44\\/e351dfc3086c55f90b596ddc345929\\/w518\\/q80\\/wpopng\\/cx163\\/cy7\\/cw316\\/ch316\\/images\\/uploads\\/44e351dfc3086c55f90b596ddc345929.webp 1210w,https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/44\\/e351dfc3086c55f90b596ddc345929\\/w518\\/q80\\/wpopng\\/cx163\\/cy7\\/cw316\\/ch316\\/images\\/uploads\\/44e351dfc3086c55f90b596ddc345929.webp 1470w,https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/44\\/e351dfc3086c55f90b596ddc345929\\/w518\\/q80\\/wpopng\\/cx163\\/cy7\\/cw316\\/ch316\\/images\\/uploads\\/44e351dfc3086c55f90b596ddc345929.webp 1680w,https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/44\\/e351dfc3086c55f90b596ddc345929\\/w518\\/q80\\/wpopng\\/cx163\\/cy7\\/cw316\\/ch316\\/images\\/uploads\\/44e351dfc3086c55f90b596ddc345929.webp 1870w,https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/44\\/e351dfc3086c55f90b596ddc345929\\/w518\\/q80\\/wpopng\\/cx163\\/cy7\\/cw316\\/ch316\\/images\\/uploads\\/44e351dfc3086c55f90b596ddc345929.webp 2048w,https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/44\\/e351dfc3086c55f90b596ddc345929\\/w518\\/q80\\/wpopng\\/cx163\\/cy7\\/cw316\\/ch316\\/images\\/uploads\\/44e351dfc3086c55f90b596ddc345929.webp 2880w\\\"\",\"image_alt\":\"\",\"image_cap\":\"\",\"image_data\":[\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/44\\/e351dfc3086c55f90b596ddc345929\\/w518\\/q80\\/wpopng\\/cx163\\/cy7\\/cw316\\/ch316\\/images\\/uploads\\/44e351dfc3086c55f90b596ddc345929.webp 880w\",\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/44\\/e351dfc3086c55f90b596ddc345929\\/w518\\/q80\\/wpopng\\/cx163\\/cy7\\/cw316\\/ch316\\/images\\/uploads\\/44e351dfc3086c55f90b596ddc345929.webp 1210w\",\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/44\\/e351dfc3086c55f90b596ddc345929\\/w518\\/q80\\/wpopng\\/cx163\\/cy7\\/cw316\\/ch316\\/images\\/uploads\\/44e351dfc3086c55f90b596ddc345929.webp 1470w\",\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/44\\/e351dfc3086c55f90b596ddc345929\\/w518\\/q80\\/wpopng\\/cx163\\/cy7\\/cw316\\/ch316\\/images\\/uploads\\/44e351dfc3086c55f90b596ddc345929.webp 1680w\",\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/44\\/e351dfc3086c55f90b596ddc345929\\/w518\\/q80\\/wpopng\\/cx163\\/cy7\\/cw316\\/ch316\\/images\\/uploads\\/44e351dfc3086c55f90b596ddc345929.webp 1870w\",\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/44\\/e351dfc3086c55f90b596ddc345929\\/w518\\/q80\\/wpopng\\/cx163\\/cy7\\/cw316\\/ch316\\/images\\/uploads\\/44e351dfc3086c55f90b596ddc345929.webp 2048w\",\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/44\\/e351dfc3086c55f90b596ddc345929\\/w518\\/q80\\/wpopng\\/cx163\\/cy7\\/cw316\\/ch316\\/images\\/uploads\\/44e351dfc3086c55f90b596ddc345929.webp 2880w\"],\"focal_point\":[\"50\",\"50\"],\"search_text\":\"The Riverside Writers Group is a five month writer's cohort launched at Riverside Studios in February 2026, led by actor, writer, and award winning facilitator\\u00a0Nadine\\u00a0Gray.The programme brings together eight emerging playwrights who have spent the past five months developing new theatrical work through a combination of group workshops, and 1:1 mentoring by\\u00a0Nadine.Throughout the programme, writers have explored character, dialogue, structure, subtext, world building, and storytelling, while developing their plays within a supportive and collaborative creative environment.\\u00a0The Riverside Writers Group Showcase will take place across two evenings, with the cohort split across both performances. Four writers will present their work on the first evening, with the remaining four writers presenting on the second evening.Across the two nights, audiences will experience excerpts from eight original new plays-in-development, with each writer presenting a 20\\u201330 minute section of their work.The showcase is an opportunity for audiences to experience exciting new writing at an early stage of development, while also giving the writers the chance to gain feedback that will support the continued growth of their work from extract to full length play.\\u00a0Showcase 1 - Saturday 18th July 19:00Your Neighbour By Nayib Jean BaptisteAn Tobar (Scots Gaelic: The Well) By Oli FyneThey\\u00a0Say They're Lesbians By Willow DaviesSESSIONS By Zainab Swanzy*This is not the running order*\\u00a0Showcase 2 - Sunday 19th July 19:00Angel By Jonas FeindReally? By Kiko ItasakaBig Tic Energy By Grace Rich\\u00a0Dolphins\\u00a0By\\u00a0Set Myint*This is not the running order*\",\"book_link\":false,\"event_type\":[\"3\"],\"search\":\"Riverside Writers Group Showcase 2026 Riverside Writers Group Showcase 2026 Theatre  <p>The<strong> Riverside Writers Group <\\/strong>is a five month writer's cohort launched at Riverside Studios in February 2026, led by actor, writer, and award winning facilitator&nbsp;<strong>Nadine&nbsp;Gray<\\/strong>.<\\/p><p>The programme brings together eight emerging playwrights who have spent the past five months developing new theatrical work through a combination of group workshops, and 1:1 mentoring by&nbsp;Nadine.<\\/p><p>Throughout the programme, writers have explored character, dialogue, structure, subtext, world building, and storytelling, while developing their plays within a supportive and collaborative creative environment.<\\/p><p>&nbsp;<\\/p><p>The Riverside Writers Group Showcase will take place across two evenings, with the cohort split across both performances. Four writers will present their work on the first evening, with the remaining four writers presenting on the second evening.<\\/p><p>Across the two nights, audiences will experience excerpts from eight original new plays-in-development, with each writer presenting a 20\\u201330 minute section of their work.<\\/p><p>The showcase is an opportunity for audiences to experience exciting new writing at an early stage of development, while also giving the writers the chance to gain feedback that will support the continued growth of their work from extract to full length play.<\\/p><p>&nbsp;<\\/p><p><strong>Showcase 1 - Saturday 18th July 19:00<\\/strong><\\/p><ul><li><strong>Your Neighbour <\\/strong><i>By Nayib Jean Baptiste<\\/i><\\/li><li><strong>An Tobar (Scots Gaelic: The Well) <\\/strong><i>By Oli Fyne<\\/i><\\/li><li><strong>They&nbsp;Say They're Lesbians <\\/strong><i>By Willow Davies<\\/i><\\/li><li><strong>SESSIONS <\\/strong><i>By Zainab Swanzy<\\/i><\\/li><\\/ul><p><i><strong>*This is not the running order*<\\/strong><\\/i><\\/p><p>&nbsp;<\\/p><p><strong>Showcase 2 - Sunday 19th July 19:00<\\/strong><\\/p><ul><li><strong>Angel <\\/strong><i>By Jonas Feind<\\/i><\\/li><li><strong>Really? <\\/strong><i>By Kiko Itasaka<\\/i><\\/li><li><strong>Big Tic Energy <\\/strong><i>By Grace Rich&nbsp;<\\/i><\\/li><li><strong>Dolphins&nbsp;<\\/strong><i>By&nbsp;Set Myint<\\/i><\\/li><\\/ul><p><i><strong>*This is not the running order*<\\/strong><\\/i><\\/p> Riverside Writers Showcase  The Riverside Writers Group is a five month writer's cohort launched at Riverside Studios in February 2026, led by actor, writer, and award winning facilitator\\u00a0Nadine\\u00a0Gray.The programme brings together eight emerging playwrights who have spent the past five months developing new theatrical work through a combination of group workshops, and 1:1 mentoring by\\u00a0Nadine.Throughout the programme, writers have explored character, dialogue, structure, subtext, world building, and storytelling, while developing their plays within a supportive and collaborative creative environment.\\u00a0The Riverside Writers Group Showcase will take place across two evenings, with the cohort split across both performances. Four writers will present their work on the first evening, with the remaining four writers presenting on the second evening.Across the two nights, audiences will experience excerpts from eight original new plays-in-development, with each writer presenting a 20\\u201330 minute section of their work.The showcase is an opportunity for audiences to experience exciting new writing at an early stage of development, while also giving the writers the chance to gain feedback that will support the continued growth of their work from extract to full length play.\\u00a0Showcase 1 - Saturday 18th July 19:00Your Neighbour By Nayib Jean BaptisteAn Tobar (Scots Gaelic: The Well) By Oli FyneThey\\u00a0Say They're Lesbians By Willow DaviesSESSIONS By Zainab Swanzy*This is not the running order*\\u00a0Showcase 2 - Sunday 19th July 19:00Angel By Jonas FeindReally? By Kiko ItasakaBig Tic Energy By Grace Rich\\u00a0Dolphins\\u00a0By\\u00a0Set Myint*This is not the running order* Theatre\"},{\"url\":\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/whats-on\\/uPd-kids-club-the-super-mario-galaxy-movie\\/\",\"id\":\"4032\",\"name\":\"Kids' Club: The Super Mario Galaxy Movie\",\"title\":\"Kids' Club: The Super Mario Galaxy Movie\",\"duration\":\"\",\"slot_tag\":\"Cinema\",\"link_title\":\"More Info\",\"performances\":{\"1784934000\":[{\"tag_ids\":[\"101\",\"81002\",\"81005\",\"80879\"],\"tag_name\":\"\",\"html\":\"<a class=\\\"performance button\\\" href=\\\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.c