c0d4eb0e33b35eebaf58fbdb11ce10a5.webp 1210w\",\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/c0\\/d4eb0e33b35eebaf58fbdb11ce10a5\\/w1470\\/q80\\/wpoJPG\\/cx670\\/cy62\\/cw1928\\/ch1925\\/images\\/uploads\\/c0d4eb0e33b35eebaf58fbdb11ce10a5.webp 1470w\",\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/c0\\/d4eb0e33b35eebaf58fbdb11ce10a5\\/w1680\\/q80\\/wpoJPG\\/cx670\\/cy62\\/cw1928\\/ch1925\\/images\\/uploads\\/c0d4eb0e33b35eebaf58fbdb11ce10a5.webp 1680w\",\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/c0\\/d4eb0e33b35eebaf58fbdb11ce10a5\\/w1870\\/q80\\/wpoJPG\\/cx670\\/cy62\\/cw1928\\/ch1925\\/images\\/uploads\\/c0d4eb0e33b35eebaf58fbdb11ce10a5.webp 1870w\",\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/c0\\/d4eb0e33b35eebaf58fbdb11ce10a5\\/w2048\\/q80\\/wpoJPG\\/cx670\\/cy62\\/cw1928\\/ch1925\\/images\\/uploads\\/c0d4eb0e33b35eebaf58fbdb11ce10a5.webp 2048w\",\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/c0\\/d4eb0e33b35eebaf58fbdb11ce10a5\\/w2880\\/q80\\/wpoJPG\\/cx670\\/cy62\\/cw1928\\/ch1925\\/images\\/uploads\\/c0d4eb0e33b35eebaf58fbdb11ce10a5.webp 2880w\"],\"focal_point\":[\"48.9\",\"43.6\"],\"search_text\":\"As master filmmaker Christopher Nolan finally reveals his ambitious take on Homer's epic THE ODYSSEY this July, travel back with us through the ages to explore how other filmmakers have drawn on the ancient myths of yesterday to forge groundbreaking big screen entertainment. Enjoy a multi-buy offer for all films in the MYTHS AND MONSTERS season with 15% off adult and concession prices if more than one ticket is purchased in same order.\\u00a0MYTHS AND MONSTERS classic film season at Riverside Studios:Clash of the Titans (1981): 18th-20th JulySpartacus (1960): 25-28th JulyTroy (2004): 1st-3rd August\\u00a0SPARTACUS (1960)\\\"One of the greatest Hollywood epics\\\" - Guardian FilmFuture 2001: A Space Odyssey director Stanley Kubrick teamed up with acting titan Kirk Douglas to deliver one of the most beloved films in the 'swords and sandals' mode in SPARTACUS. The film earned six Academy Award nominations and won four of them.The rebellious Thracian Spartacus (Douglas), born and raised a slave, is sold to Gladiator trainer Batiatus. After weeks of being trained to kill for the arena, Spartacus turns on his owners and leads the other slaves in rebellion. As the rebels move from town to town, their numbers swell as escaped slaves join their ranks. Under the leadership of Spartacus, they make their way to southern Italy, where they will cross the sea and return to their homes.Age Rating:PGLanguage:EnglishContent Warnings:Contains moderate violenceDirector:Stnaley KubrickCast:Kirk Douglas, Laurence Olivier, Jean Simmons, Peter UstimovCompany:Park CircusTrailers:20 minsYear of Release:1960\",\"book_link\":false,\"cinema\":[\"81024\"],\"event_type\":[\"101\"],\"event_age_ratings\":[\"81002\"],\"search\":\"Spartacus Spartacus Cinema  <p>As master filmmaker Christopher Nolan finally reveals his ambitious take on Homer's epic <i>THE ODYSSEY<\\/i> this July, travel back with us through the ages to explore how other filmmakers have drawn on the ancient myths of yesterday to forge groundbreaking big screen entertainment. Enjoy a multi-buy offer for all films in the <strong>MYTHS AND MONSTERS<\\/strong> season with 15% off adult and concession prices if more than one ticket is purchased in same order.<\\/p><p>&nbsp;<\\/p><p><strong>MYTHS AND MONSTERS <\\/strong>classic film season at Riverside Studios:<\\/p><p><i>Clash of the Titans<\\/i> (1981): 18th-20th July<\\/p><p><i>Spartacus<\\/i> (1960): 25-28th July<\\/p><p><i>Troy <\\/i>(2004): 1st-3rd August<\\/p><p>&nbsp;<\\/p><p><i><strong>SPARTACUS <\\/strong><\\/i><strong>(1960)<\\/strong><\\/p><blockquote><p>\\\"One of the greatest Hollywood epics\\\" - Guardian Film<\\/p><\\/blockquote><p>Future <i>2001: A Space Odyssey<\\/i> director Stanley Kubrick teamed up with acting titan Kirk Douglas to deliver one of the most beloved films in the 'swords and sandals' mode in <i><strong>SPARTACUS<\\/strong><\\/i>. The film earned six Academy Award nominations and won four of them.<\\/p><p>The rebellious Thracian Spartacus (Douglas), born and raised a slave, is sold to Gladiator trainer Batiatus. After weeks of being trained to kill for the arena, Spartacus turns on his owners and leads the other slaves in rebellion. As the rebels move from town to town, their numbers swell as escaped slaves join their ranks. Under the leadership of Spartacus, they make their way to southern Italy, where they will cross the sea and return to their homes.<\\/p><figure class=\\\"table\\\"><table><tbody><tr><td><strong>Age Rating:<\\/strong><\\/td><td>PG<\\/td><\\/tr><tr><td><strong>Language:<\\/strong><\\/td><td>English<\\/td><\\/tr><tr><td><strong>Content Warnings:<\\/strong><\\/td><td>Contains moderate violence<\\/td><\\/tr><tr><td><strong>Director:<\\/strong><\\/td><td>Stnaley Kubrick<\\/td><\\/tr><tr><td><strong>Cast:<\\/strong><\\/td><td>Kirk Douglas, Laurence Olivier, Jean Simmons, Peter Ustimov<\\/td><\\/tr><tr><td><strong>Company:<\\/strong><\\/td><td>Park Circus<\\/td><\\/tr><tr><td><strong>Trailers:<\\/strong><\\/td><td>20 mins<\\/td><\\/tr><tr><td><strong>Year of Release:<\\/strong><\\/td><td>1960<\\/td><\\/tr><\\/tbody><\\/table><\\/figure> Spartacus  As master filmmaker Christopher Nolan finally reveals his ambitious take on Homer's epic THE ODYSSEY this July, travel back with us through the ages to explore how other filmmakers have drawn on the ancient myths of yesterday to forge groundbreaking big screen entertainment. Enjoy a multi-buy offer for all films in the MYTHS AND MONSTERS season with 15% off adult and concession prices if more than one ticket is purchased in same order.\\u00a0MYTHS AND MONSTERS classic film season at Riverside Studios:Clash of the Titans (1981): 18th-20th JulySpartacus (1960): 25-28th JulyTroy (2004): 1st-3rd August\\u00a0SPARTACUS (1960)\\\"One of the greatest Hollywood epics\\\" - 