6479635b9a1fe5.webp 2048w\",\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/30\\/f758b2c563f9a1836479635b9a1fe5\\/w800\\/q80\\/wpopng\\/images\\/uploads\\/30f758b2c563f9a1836479635b9a1fe5.webp 2880w\"],\"focal_point\":[\"50\",\"50\"],\"search_text\":\"A moving\\u202fdrama set during the Biafran War of the 1960s and post-war Nigeria of the 1970s, following childhood friends Ade and Tolu as they come of age in a world shaped by conflict. The play explores friendship,\\u202fidentity\\u202fand the lasting impact of war, asking whether two people with opposing beliefs can remain connected as they grow into\\u202fadulthood.\\u00a0Follow @splinteredplay-Emeka Diamond (Writer & Producer)-Isabel Steuble-Johnson (Director)-Michelle Aramid\\u00e9 (Producer)-Danny Jeffs (Assistant Director)-Atlanta Sonson-Chapman (Lighting Designer\\/Lighting Operator)-Isabella Sarmiento (Set Designer)-Sabrina Bear Sam (Dramaturg)-Femi Olajugbagbe (Movement Director)-Gwent Odai: Playing \\\"Ade\\\"-Daniel Abeshin: Playing \\\"Tolu\\\"\",\"book_link\":false,\"event_type\":[\"81021\"],\"search\":\"Splintered Splintered Bitesize  <p>A moving\\u202fdrama set during the Biafran War of the 1960s and post-war Nigeria of the 1970s, following childhood friends Ade and Tolu as they come of age in a world shaped by conflict. The play explores friendship,\\u202fidentity\\u202fand the lasting impact of war, asking whether two people with opposing beliefs can remain connected as they grow into\\u202fadulthood.<\\/p><p>&nbsp;<\\/p><p>Follow <strong>@splinteredplay<\\/strong><\\/p><p>-Emeka Diamond (Writer &amp; Producer)<\\/p><p>-Isabel Steuble-Johnson (Director)<\\/p><p>-Michelle Aramid\\u00e9 (Producer)<\\/p><p>-Danny Jeffs (Assistant Director)<\\/p><p>-Atlanta Sonson-Chapman (Lighting Designer\\/Lighting Operator)<\\/p><p>-Isabella Sarmiento (Set Designer)<\\/p><p>-Sabrina Bear Sam (Dramaturg)<\\/p><p>-Femi Olajugbagbe (Movement Director)<\\/p><p>-Gwent Odai: Playing \\\"Ade\\\"<\\/p><p>-Daniel Abeshin: Playing \\\"Tolu\\\"<\\/p> Splintered  A moving\\u202fdrama set during the Biafran War of the 1960s and post-war Nigeria of the 1970s, following childhood friends Ade and Tolu as they come of age in a world shaped by conflict. The play explores friendship,\\u202fidentity\\u202fand the lasting impact of war, asking whether two people with opposing beliefs can remain connected as they grow into\\u202fadulthood.\\u00a0Follow @splinteredplay-Emeka Diamond (Writer & Producer)-Isabel Steuble-Johnson (Director)-Michelle Aramid\\u00e9 (Producer)-Danny Jeffs (Assistant Director)-Atlanta Sonson-Chapman (Lighting Designer\\/Lighting Operator)-Isabella Sarmiento (Set Designer)-Sabrina Bear Sam (Dramaturg)-Femi Olajugbagbe (Movement Director)-Gwent Odai: Playing \\\"Ade\\\"-Daniel Abeshin: Playing \\\"Tolu\\\" Bitesize\"},{\"url\":\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/whats-on\\/YL-little-lord-fondleroy\\/\",\"id\":\"3728\",\"name\":\"Little Lord Fondleroy\",\"title\":\"Little Lord Fondleroy\",\"duration\":\"60 minutes\",\"slot_tag\":\"Bitesize\",\"link_title\":\"More Info\",\"performances\":{\"1787094000\":[{\"tag_ids\":[\"81021\"],\"tag_name\":\"\",\"html\":\"<a class=\\\"performance button\\\" href=\\\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/seats\\/232816\\/\\\">\\n   \\n      <div class=\\\"performance-time\\\" data-acc=\\\"\\\">14:00<\\/div>\\n    \\n<\\/a>\\n\",\"timestamp\":\"1787144400\",\"accessibility_class\":\"\"},{\"tag_ids\":[\"81021\"],\"tag_name\":\"\",\"html\":\"<a class=\\\"performance button\\\" href=\\\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/seats\\/233602\\/\\\">\\n   \\n      <div class=\\\"performance-time\\\" data-acc=\\\"\\\">20:45<\\/div>\\n    \\n<\\/a>\\n\",\"timestamp\":\"1787168700\",\"accessibility_class\":\"\"}],\"1787353200\":[{\"tag_ids\":[\"81021\"],\"tag_name\":\"\",\"html\":\"<a class=\\\"performance button\\\" href=\\\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/seats\\/233003\\/\\\">\\n   \\n      <div class=\\\"performance-time\\\" data-acc=\\