\\\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/ae\\/73b12f2bff150de98e960919d4f572\\/w880\\/q80\\/wpopng\\/cx242\\/cw1026\\/ch1024\\/images\\/uploads\\/ae73b12f2bff150de98e960919d4f572.webp 880w,https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/ae\\/73b12f2bff150de98e960919d4f572\\/w1210\\/q80\\/wpopng\\/cx242\\/cw1026\\/ch1024\\/images\\/uploads\\/ae73b12f2bff150de98e960919d4f572.webp 1210w,https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/ae\\/73b12f2bff150de98e960919d4f572\\/w1470\\/q80\\/wpopng\\/cx242\\/cw1026\\/ch1024\\/images\\/uploads\\/ae73b12f2bff150de98e960919d4f572.webp 1470w,https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/ae\\/73b12f2bff150de98e960919d4f572\\/w1536\\/q80\\/wpopng\\/cx242\\/cw1026\\/ch1024\\/images\\/uploads\\/ae73b12f2bff150de98e960919d4f572.webp 1680w,https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/ae\\/73b12f2bff150de98e960919d4f572\\/w1536\\/q80\\/wpopng\\/cx242\\/cw1026\\/ch1024\\/images\\/uploads\\/ae73b12f2bff150de98e960919d4f572.webp 1870w,https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/ae\\/73b12f2bff150de98e960919d4f572\\/w1536\\/q80\\/wpopng\\/cx242\\/cw1026\\/ch1024\\/images\\/uploads\\/ae73b12f2bff150de98e960919d4f572.webp 2048w,https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/ae\\/73b12f2bff150de98e960919d4f572\\/w1536\\/q80\\/wpopng\\/cx242\\/cw1026\\/ch1024\\/images\\/uploads\\/ae73b12f2bff150de98e960919d4f572.webp 2880w\\\"\",\"image_alt\":\"\",\"image_cap\":\"\",\"image_data\":[\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/ae\\/73b12f2bff150de98e960919d4f572\\/w880\\/q80\\/wpopng\\/cx242\\/cw1026\\/ch1024\\/images\\/uploads\\/ae73b12f2bff150de98e960919d4f572.webp 880w\",\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/ae\\/73b12f2bff150de98e960919d4f572\\/w1210\\/q80\\/wpopng\\/cx242\\/cw1026\\/ch1024\\/images\\/uploads\\/ae73b12f2bff150de98e960919d4f572.webp 1210w\",\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/ae\\/73b12f2bff150de98e960919d4f572\\/w1470\\/q80\\/wpopng\\/cx242\\/cw1026\\/ch1024\\/images\\/uploads\\/ae73b12f2bff150de98e960919d4f572.webp 1470w\",\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/ae\\/73b12f2bff150de98e960919d4f572\\/w1536\\/q80\\/wpopng\\/cx242\\/cw1026\\/ch1024\\/images\\/uploads\\/ae73b12f2bff150de98e960919d4f572.webp 1680w\",\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/ae\\/73b12f2bff150de98e960919d4f572\\/w1536\\/q80\\/wpopng\\/cx242\\/cw1026\\/ch1024\\/images\\/uploads\\/ae73b12f2bff150de98e960919d4f572.webp 1870w\",\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/ae\\/73b12f2bff150de98e960919d4f572\\/w1536\\/q80\\/wpopng\\/cx242\\/cw1026\\/ch1024\\/images\\/uploads\\/ae73b12f2bff150de98e960919d4f572.webp 2048w\",\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/ae\\/73b12f2bff150de98e960919d4f572\\/w1536\\/q80\\/wpopng\\/cx242\\/cw1026\\/ch1024\\/images\\/uploads\\/ae73b12f2bff150de98e960919d4f572.webp 2880w\"],\"focal_point\":[\"48.4\",\"33.6\"],\"search_text\":\"Are You Even Indian? follows a British-born Indian woman and an Indian-born man who fall in love. It feels like fate. A meet-cute, wedding dances, Bollywood jokes, and plans for a future they believe they are building together.But as the relationship deepens, so do the cracks. Which country is \\u201chome\\u201d? What language will their child speak? Who gets to decide what makes someone truly Indian?\\u00a0As personal choices clash with family expectations and social labels, the couple must confront love, compromise, and the reality of living in between. Neither fully British, nor fully Indian, the show reflects the experience of a generation navigating relationships and heritage.When both your homes ask you to apologise for who you are, how do you decide where you belong?This is a love story about proving your identity, not just to each other, but within the community.\\\"Highly Recommended\\\" - FringeReview\\u2605\\u2605\\u2605\\u2605 \\\"A quite excellent and nuanced production\\\" -\\u00a0 Rialto Arts\\u2605\\u2605\\u2605\\u2605 \\\"Feels genuine, relatable and, at times, uncomfortably honest\\\" - Sussex News\\\"A gripping and culturally insightful piece of dance-theatre\\\" - Step Behind the Stage\\u00a0Best Show, Bitesize Festival (Riverside Studios) 2025Highly recommended show (Brighton Fringe) 2026Shortlist for Best New writing (Brighton Fringe) 2026\",\"book_link\":false,\"event_type\":[\"3\"],\"search\":\"Are You Even Indian? Are You Even Indian? Theatre  <p><i><strong>Are You Even Indian?<\\/strong><\\/i> follows a British-born Indian woman and an Indian-born man who fall in love. It feels like fate. A meet-cute, wedding dances, Bollywood jokes, and plans for a future they believe they are building together.<\\/p><p>But as the relationship deepens, so do the cracks. Which country is \\u201chome\\u201d? What language will their child speak? Who gets to decide what makes someone truly Indian?<br>&nbsp;<\\/p><p>As personal choices clash with family expectations and social labels, the couple must confront love, compromise, and the reality of living in between. Neither fully British, nor fully Indian, the show reflects the experience of a generation navigating relationships and heritage.<\\/p><p><br>When both your homes ask you to apologise for who you are, how do you decide where you belong?<\\/p><p><br>This is a love story about proving your identity, not just to each other, but within the community.<\\/p><blockquote><p><br><strong>\\\"Highly Recommended\\\" - <\\/strong>FringeReview<\\/p><p><strong>\\u2605\\u2605\\u2605\\u2605 \\\"A quite excellent and nuanced production\\\" -&nbsp; <\\/strong>Rialto Arts<\\/p><p><strong>\\u2605\\u2605\\u2605\\u2605 \\\"Feels genuine, relatable and, at times, uncomfortably honest\\\" - <\\/strong>Sussex News<\\/p><p><strong>\\\"A gripping and culturally insightful piece of dance-theatre\\\"<\\/strong> - Step Behind the Stage<br>&nbsp;<\\/p><\\/blockquote><p><strong>Best Show, Bitesize Festival (Riverside Studios) 2025<\\/strong><\\/p><p><strong>Highly recommended show (Brighton Fringe) 2026<\\/strong><\\/p><p><strong>Shortlist for Best New writing (Brighton Fringe) 2026<\\/strong><\\/p> Are You Even Indian?  Are You Even Indian? follows a British-born Indian woman and an Indian-born man who fall in love. It feels like fate. A meet-cute, wedding dances, Bollywood jokes, and plans for a future they believe they are building together.But as the relationship deepens, so do the cracks. Which country is \\u201chome\\u201d? What language will their child speak? Who gets to decide what makes someone truly Indian?\\u00a0As personal choices clash with family expectations and social labels, the couple must confront love, compromise, and the reality of living in between. Neither fully British, nor fully Indian, the show reflects the experience of a generation navigating relationships and heritage.When both your homes ask you to apologise for who you are, how do you decide where you belong?This is a love story about proving your identity, not just to each other, but within the community.\\\"Highly Recommended\\\" - FringeReview\\u2605\\u2605\\u2605\\u2605 \\\"A quite excellent and nuanced production\\\" -\\u00a0 Rialto Arts\\u2605\\u2605\\u2605\\u2605 \\\"Feels genuine, relatable and, at times, uncomfortably honest\\\" - Sussex News\\\"A gripping and culturally insightful piece of dance-theatre\\\" - Step Behind the Stage\\u00a0Best Show, Bitesize Festival (Riverside Studios) 2025Highly recommended show (Brighton Fringe) 2026Shortlist for Best New writing (Brighton Fringe) 2026 Theatre\"},{\"url\":\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/whats-on\\/uPX-cradle-stories-of-iran-exile-belonging\\/\",\"id\":\"4081\",\"name\":\"Cradle: Stories of Iran, Exile & Belonging\",\"title\":\"Cradle: Stories of Iran, Exile & Belonging\",\"duration\":\"240 minutes\",\"slot_tag\":\"Theatre\",\"link_title\":\"More Info\",\"performances\":{\"1795305600\":[{\"tag_ids\":[\"3\"],\"tag_name\":\"\",\"html\":\"<a class=\\\"performance button\\\" href=\\\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/seats\\/257403\\/\\\">\\n   \\n      <div class=\\\"performance-time\\\" data-acc=\\\"\\\">14:30<\\/div>\\n    \\n<\\/a>\\n\",\"timestamp\":\"1795357800\",\"accessibility_class\":\"\"}]},\"performance_dates\":[1795305600],\"times\":[1795357800],\"start_date\":\"1795357800\",\"end_date\":\"1795357800\",\"age_rating_class\":\"\",\"ticket_free\":false,\"priority_booking\":true,\"hash\":\"dE1DbFZxQVYwVlFrUUFzVDhRcGdaZz09\",\"embed_id\":\"\",\"embed_host\":\"\",\"date_formatted\":\"Sun 22 Nov 2026\",\"text\":\"Mandi Riggi (Tribe Collective) and Claudia Vyvyan (Kick The Door Down)&nbsp;present a festival of short plays. 8 writers and their teams will rehearse&hellip;\",\"image_url\":\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/67\\/7d9c04338c8ca9210728eef51f5ef5\\/w880\\/q80\\/cx444\\/cw916\\/ch912\\/images\\/uploads\\/677d9c04338c8ca9210728eef51f5ef5.jpeg\",\"image_source\":\"type=\\\"image\\/webp\\\" srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/67\\/7d9c04338c8ca9210728eef51f5ef5\\/w880\\/q80\\/wpojpeg\\/cx444\\/cw916\\/ch912\\/images\\/uploads\\/677d9c04338c8ca9210728eef51f5ef5.webp 880w,https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/67\\/7d9c04338c8ca9210728eef51f5ef5\\/w1210\\/q80\\/wpojpeg\\/cx444\\/cw916\\/ch912\\/images\\/uploads\\/677d9c04338c8ca9210728eef51f5ef5.webp 1210w,https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/67\\/7d9c04338c8ca9210728eef51f5ef5\\/w1470\\/q80\\/wpojpeg\\/cx444\\/cw916\\/ch912\\/images\\/uploads\\/677d9c04338c8ca9210728eef51f5ef5.webp 1470w,https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/67\\/7d9c04338c8ca9210728eef51f5ef5\\/w1680\\/q80\\/wpojpeg\\/cx444\\/cw916\\/ch912\\/images\\/uploads\\/677d9c04338c8ca9210728eef51f5ef5.webp 1680w,https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/67\\/7d9c04338c8ca9210728eef51f5ef5\\/w1720\\/q80\\/wpojpeg\\/cx444\\/cw916\\/ch912\\/images\\/uploads\\/677d9c04338c8ca9210728eef51f5ef5.webp 1870w,https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/67\\/7d9c04338c8ca9210728eef51f5ef5\\/w1720\\/q80\\/wpojpeg\\/cx444\\/cw916\\/ch912\\/images\\/uploads\\/677d9c04338c8ca9210728eef51f5ef5.webp 2048w,https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/67\\/7d9c04338c8ca9210728eef51f5ef5\\/w1720\\/q80\\/wpojpeg\\/cx444\\/cw916\\/ch912\\/images\\/uploads\\/677d9c04338c8ca9210728eef51f5ef5.webp 2880w\\\"\",\"image_alt\":\"\",\"image_cap\":\"\",\"image_data\":[\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/67\\/7d9c04338c8ca9210728eef51f5ef5\\/w880\\/q80\\/wpojpeg\\/cx444\\/cw916\\/ch912\\/images\\/uploads\\/677d9c04338c8ca9210728eef51f5ef5.webp 880w\",\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/67\\/7d9c04338c8ca9210728eef51f5ef5\\/w1210\\/q80\\/wpojpeg\\/cx444\\/cw916\\/ch912\\/images\\/uploads\\/677d9c04338c8ca9210728eef51f5ef5.webp 1210w\",\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/67\\/7d9c04338c8ca9210728eef51f5ef5\\/w1470\\/q80\\/wpojpeg\\/cx444\\/cw916\\/ch912\\/images\\/uploads\\/677d9c04338c8ca9210728eef51f5ef5.webp 1470w\",\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/67\\/7d9c04338c8ca9210728eef51f5ef5\\/w1680\\/q80\\/wpojpeg\\/cx444\\/cw916\\/ch912\\/images\\/uploads\\/677d9c04338c8ca9210728eef51f5ef5.webp 1680w\",\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/67\\/7d9c04338c8ca9210728eef51f5ef5\\/w1720\\/q80\\/wpojpeg\\/cx444\\/cw916\\/ch912\\/images\\/uploads\\/677d9c04338c8ca9210728eef51f5ef5.webp 1870w\",\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/67\\/7d9c04338c8ca9210728eef51f5ef5\\/w1720\\/q80\\/wpojpeg\\/cx444\\/cw916\\/ch912\\/images\\/uploads\\/677d9c04338c8ca9210728eef51f5ef5.webp 2048w\",\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/67\\/7d9c04338c8ca9210728eef51f5ef5\\/w1720\\/q80\\/wpojpeg\\/cx444\\/cw916\\/ch912\\/images\\/uploads\\/677d9c04338c8ca9210728eef51f5ef5.webp 2880w\"],\"focal_point\":[\"50.4\",\"43.3\"],\"search_text\":\"Mandi Riggi (Tribe Collective) and Claudia Vyvyan (Kick The Door Down)\\u00a0present a festival of short plays. 8 writers and their teams will rehearse for a week before debuting on stage in a relaxed sharing of Iranian community, culture and creative talent. The festival aims to broaden understanding of Iranian stories beyond the diaspora.\\u00a0Each play will include at least one Iranian creative, whether as a writer, director or actor, ensuring the work remains rooted in lived experience and cultural knowledge. Around that, we have built genuinely collaborative creative teams that bring together artists from different backgrounds. The goal is to create a space where Iranian stories become part of a wider cultural conversation. Rather than speaking only to our own community, CRADLE invites artists and audiences from outside that experience to engage with these stories thoughtfully, guided by Iranian collaborators.For us, that's where theatre is at its most powerful: not reinforcing cultural boundaries but creating meaningful dialogue across them. We don't believe stories should remain inside the communities they originate from. We believe they should travel like we do.\",\"book_link\":\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/seats\\/257403\\/\",\"event_type\":[\"3\"],\"search\":\"Cradle: Stories of Iran, Exile & Belonging Cradle: Stories of Iran, Exile & Belonging Theatre  <p>Mandi Riggi (Tribe Collective) and Claudia Vyvyan (Kick The Door Down)&nbsp;present a festival of short plays. 8 writers and their teams will rehearse for a week before debuting on stage in a relaxed sharing of Iranian community, culture and creative talent. The festival aims to broaden understanding of Iranian stories beyond the diaspora.&nbsp;<\\/p><p>Each play will include at least one Iranian creative, whether as a writer, director or actor, ensuring the work remains rooted in lived experience and cultural knowledge. Around that, we have built genuinely collaborative creative teams that bring together artists from different backgrounds. The goal is to create a space where Iranian stories become part of a wider cultural conversation. Rather than speaking only to our own community, <i><strong>CRADLE <\\/strong><\\/i>invites artists and audiences from outside that experience to engage with these stories thoughtfully, guided by Iranian collaborators.<\\/p><p>For us, that's where theatre is at its most powerful: not reinforcing cultural boundaries but creating meaningful dialogue across them. We don't believe stories should remain inside the communities they originate from. We believe they should travel like we do.<\\/p> Cradle: Stories of Iran, Exile & Belonging  Mandi Riggi (Tribe Collective) and Claudia Vyvyan (Kick The Door Down)\\u00a0present a festival of short plays. 8 writers and their teams will rehearse for a week before debuting on stage in a relaxed sharing of Iranian community, culture and creative talent. The festival aims to broaden understanding of Iranian stories beyond the diaspora.\\u00a0Each play will include at least one Iranian creative, whether as a writer, director or actor, ensuring the work remains rooted in lived experience and cultural knowledge. Around that, we have built genuinely collaborative creative teams that bring together artists from different backgrounds. The goal is to create a space where Iranian stories become part of a wider cultural conversation. Rather than speaking only to our own community, CRADLE invites artists and audiences from outside that experience to engage with these stories thoughtfully, guided by Iranian collaborators.For us, that's where theatre is at its most powerful: not reinforcing cultural boundaries but creating meaningful dialogue across them. We don't believe stories should remain inside the communities they originate from. We believe they should travel like we do. Theatre\"},{\"url\":\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/whats-on\\/aY-the-mainstage-prize\\/\",\"id\":\"3098\",\"name\":\"The Mainstage Prize\",\"title\":\"The Mainstage Prize\",\"duration\":\"150 minutes\",\"slot_tag\":\"Theatre\",\"link_title\":\"More Info\",\"performances\":{\"1803254400\":[{\"tag_ids\":[\"80951\",\"3\"],\"tag_name\":\"\",\"html\":\"<a class=\\\"performance button\\\" href=\\\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/seats\\/193601\\/\\\">\\n   \\n      <div class=\\\"performance-time\\\" data-acc=\\\"\\\">19:00<\\/div>\\n    \\n<\\/a>\\n\",\"timestamp\":\"1803322800\",\"accessibility_class\":\"\"}]},\"performance_dates\":[1803254400],\"times\":[1803322800],\"start_date\":\"1803322800\",\"end_date\":\"1803324600\",\"age_rating_class\":\"\",\"ticket_free\":false,\"priority_booking\":true,\"hash\":\"ZFNSdGh2cjFSRXpUbkQ3YnFwVGVQUT09\",\"embed_id\":\"\",\"embed_host\":\"\",\"date_formatted\":\"Mon 22 Feb 2027\",\"text\":\"Join us for an electrifying evening of high-stakes storytelling as we crown the inaugural winner of the Mainstage Prize.At a time when the theatre industry&hellip;\",\"image_url\":\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/2f\\/580b9ba877f05aed49e3d6b2cc5ff8\\/w880\\/q80\\/images\\/uploads\\/2f580b9ba877f05aed49e3d6b2cc5ff8.png\",\"image_source\":\"type=\\\"image\\/webp\\\" srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/2f\\/580b9ba877f05aed49e3d6b2cc5ff8\\/w880\\/q80\\/wpopng\\/images\\/uploads\\/2f580b9ba877f05aed49e3d6b2cc5ff8.webp 880w,https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/2f\\/580b9ba877f05aed49e3d6b2cc5ff8\\/w1137\\/q80\\/wpopng\\/images\\/uploads\\/2f580b9ba877f05aed49e3d6b2cc5ff8.webp 1210w,https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/2f\\/580b9ba877f05aed49e3d6b2cc5ff8\\/w1137\\/q80\\/wpopng\\/images\\/uploads\\/2f580b9ba877f05aed49e3d6b2cc5ff8.webp 1470w,https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/2f\\/580b9ba877f05aed49e3d6b2cc5ff8\\/w1137\\/q80\\/wpopng\\/images\\/uploads\\/2f580b9ba877f05aed49e3d6b2cc5ff8.webp 1680w,https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/2f\\/580b9ba877f05aed49e3d6b2cc5ff8\\/w1137\\/q80\\/wpopng\\/images\\/uploads\\/2f580b9ba877f05aed49e3d6b2cc5ff8.webp 1870w,https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/2f\\/580b9ba877f05aed49e3d6b2cc5ff8\\/w1137\\/q80\\/wpopng\\/images\\/uploads\\/2f580b9ba877f05aed49e3d6b2cc5ff8.webp 2048w,https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/2f\\/580b9ba877f05aed49e3d6b2cc5ff8\\/w1137\\/q80\\/wpopng\\/images\\/uploads\\/2f580b9ba877f05aed49e3d6b2cc5ff8.webp 2880w\\\"\",\"image_alt\":\"\",\"image_cap\":\"\",\"image_data\":[\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/2f\\/580b9ba877f05aed49e3d6b2cc5ff8\\/w880\\/q80\\/wpopng\\/images\\/uploads\\/2f580b9ba877f05aed49e3d6b2cc5ff8.webp 880w\",\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/2f\\/580b9ba877f05aed49e3d6b2cc5ff8\\/w1137\\/q80\\/wpopng\\/images\\/uploads\\/2f580b9ba877f05aed49e3d6b2cc5ff8.webp 1210w\",\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/2f\\/580b9ba877f05aed49e3d6b2cc5ff8\\/w1137\\/q80\\/wpopng\\/images\\/uploads\\/2f580b9ba877f05aed49e3d6b2cc5ff8.webp 1470w\",\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/2f\\/580b9ba877f05aed49e3d6b2cc5ff8\\/w1137\\/q80\\/wpopng\\/images\\/uploads\\/2f580b9ba877f05aed49e3d6b2cc5ff8.webp 1680w\",\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/2f\\/580b9ba877f05aed49e3d6b2cc5ff8\\/w1137\\/q80\\/wpopng\\/images\\/uploads\\/2f580b9ba877f05aed49e3d6b2cc5ff8.webp 1870w\",\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/2f\\/580b9ba877f05aed49e3d6b2cc5ff8\\/w1137\\/q80\\/wpopng\\/images\\/uploads\\/2f580b9ba877f05aed49e3d6b2cc5ff8.webp 2048w\",\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/custom\\/2f\\/580b9ba877f05aed49e3d6b2cc5ff8\\/w1137\\/q80\\/wpopng\\/images\\/uploads\\/2f580b9ba877f05aed49e3d6b2cc5ff8.webp 2880w\"],\"focal_point\":[\"50\",\"50\"],\"search_text\":\"Join us for an electrifying evening of high-stakes storytelling as we crown the inaugural winner of the Mainstage Prize.At a time when the theatre industry is hungry for work that revitalizes audience attendance, the Mainstage Prize was set up to champion work with emotional weight, gripping narrative drive, and the sheer power to fill a room. We celebrate writers who think on a grand scale, crafting bold characters and ideas that spark public conversation. The winning playwright recieves a \\u00a310,000 cash prize and mentorship opportunities with leading industry figures.\\u00a0Each year the Prize will focus on a different topic or genre, inviting playwrights to work with it as a storytelling engine. This year, the Prize's focus is Horror.\\u00a0\\u00a0The evening will feature professional rehearsed readings of our three finalist plays, offering you the very first glimpse into these gripping, spooky new works, before we announce the winner at the end of the night.\\u00a0\",\"book_link\":\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/seats\\/193601\\/\",\"event_type\":[\"3\",\"80951\"],\"search\":\"The Mainstage Prize The Mainstage Prize Theatre  <p>Join us for an electrifying evening of high-stakes storytelling as we crown the inaugural winner of the <strong>Mainstage Prize<\\/strong>.<br><br>At a time when the theatre industry is hungry for work that revitalizes audience attendance, the Mainstage Prize was set up to champion work with emotional weight, gripping narrative drive, and the sheer power to fill a room. We celebrate writers who think on a grand scale, crafting bold characters and ideas that spark public conversation. The winning playwright recieves a \\u00a310,000 cash prize and mentorship opportunities with leading industry figures.&nbsp;<br><br>Each year the Prize will focus on a different topic or genre, inviting playwrights to work with it as a storytelling engine. This year, the Prize's focus is <strong>Horror<\\/strong>.&nbsp;<\\/p><p>&nbsp;<\\/p><p>The evening will feature professional rehearsed readings of our three finalist plays, offering you the very first glimpse into these gripping, spooky new works, before we announce the winner at the end of the night.&nbsp;<\\/p> The Mainstage Prize  Join us for an electrifying evening of high-stakes storytelling as we crown the inaugural winner of the Mainstage Prize.At a time when the theatre industry is hungry for work that revitalizes audience attendance, the Mainstage Prize was set up to champion work with emotional weight, gripping narrative drive, and the sheer power to fill a room. We celebrate writers who think on a grand scale, crafting bold characters and ideas that spark public conversation. The winning playwright recieves a \\u00a310,000 cash prize and mentorship opportunities with leading industry figures.\\u00a0Each year the Prize will focus on a different topic or genre, inviting playwrights to work with it as a storytelling engine. This year, the Prize's focus is Horror.\\u00a0\\u00a0The evening will feature professional rehearsed readings of our three finalist plays, offering you the very first glimpse into these gripping, spooky new works, before we announce the winner at the end of the night.\\u00a0 Theatre Events\"}]",
